    <bpmn:process id="W_W470" name="W470. Store-Level Rotational Brownout / Power Outage Management Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Advance notification from electric utility of scheduled rotational brownout; or sudden unscheduled power outage
Frequency: Mindanao (60 stores): ~2–4 events/month per store during dry season (March–May); Visayas (40 stores): ~1–2 events/month; Luzon (100 stores): occasional, primarily during typhoon season; total chain: ~800–1,500 store-outage events/year (per the per-store rates above)
Volume: 1–30 stores affected per event (rotational brownouts affect specific feeder areas); typical duration: 2–8 hours
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Maintenance / Utility, Cashier, Department Supervisor, Security Guard
Source: workflow W470 — Store-Level Rotational Brownout / Power Outage Management Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W470_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W470_Lane1" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W470_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W470_Lane3" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W470_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W470_Start5" name="Advance notification from electric utility of scheduled rotational brownout; or sudden…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task6" name="Brownout schedule monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Brownout schedule monitoring: Maintenance / Utility staff monitors electric utility advisories (social media, SMS alerts, utility website) for scheduled rotational brownouts in the store&#x27;s area; for utilities that publish schedules, Maintenance receives schedule weekly and shares with Store Manager; for unscheduled outages, trigger is the power loss itself (step 5)
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Utility
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/week during brownout season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task7" name="Pre-outage preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-outage preparation (for scheduled brownouts): (a) Store Manager confirms generator fuel level ≥ 75%; if below, arranges emergency fuel delivery (maintain relationship with local fuel supplier); (b) Maintenance verifies generator startup (test run for 5 minutes if last test &gt; 2 weeks); (c) Maintenance confirms UPS battery charge for POS terminals (each terminal has ~15 min battery backup for graceful shutdown); (d) Store Manager briefs staff on shift: approximate outage window, which operations will be reduced
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/prep</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task8" name="Customer pre-notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer pre-notification (for scheduled brownouts): (a) Store Manager posts &quot;Scheduled Power Maintenance&quot; notice at store entrance; (b) reduced lighting areas marked; (c) PA announcement at start of outage: &quot;We are experiencing a temporary power interruption. Our store remains open. Some areas may have reduced lighting. Thank you for your patience.&quot;
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task9" name="Load priority plan execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Load priority plan execution: Store Manager activates pre-defined load priority for generator power: Priority 1 (always powered): (a) 2 of 3 POS terminals (1 terminal shut down to reduce load), (b) security system and CCTV (non-negotiable — W71 requirement), (c) emergency lighting (fire exits, main aisles), (d) fire alarm and suppression monitoring; Priority 2 (powered if generator capacity allows): (e) customer-facing display lighting (main aisles only — gallery and appliance sections deprioritized), (f) paint mixing station (high customer demand), (g) receiving dock lighting (if trucks scheduled); Priority 3 (not powered during outage): (h) backroom/stockroom lighting (use handheld flashlights), (i) office area (computers shut down), (j) air conditioning (customer discomfort is tolerable for 2–4 hours; staff use portable fans), (k) outdoor yard lighting (unless customer traffic is heavy), (l) non-essential signage
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task10" name="Unscheduled outage response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Unscheduled outage response: When power drops without warning: (a) UPS provides ~15 min battery for POS terminals — Cashier completes current transaction and logs out; (b) Maintenance starts generator (target: within 3 minutes of outage); (c) Store Manager makes PA announcement; (d) Security Guard activates handheld flashlight protocol for dark areas; (e) Department Supervisors assist customers in darker sections (tiles gallery, plumbing aisles) toward better-lit areas; (f) if generator fails to start within 10 minutes, escalate to W5E (Store Opening Delay Procedure) — consider partial store closure
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task11" name="Sensitive goods protection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Sensitive goods protection: (a) Paint and chemicals: Maintenance verifies ventilation continues (exhaust fans may be on generator backup); if ambient temperature in paint mixing area exceeds 35°C, temporarily suspend paint mixing operations; (b) Appliances: Demo units on display powered down to prevent voltage surge damage; (c) Refrigerated items (if any — limited in hardware retail): check temperature log; if outage exceeds 4 hours, disposition per food safety guidelines; (d) Lumber yard: no special action required — outdoor inventory is not power-dependent
Responsible (R): Maintenance / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task12" name="Extended outage escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Extended outage escalation (beyond 4 hours): (a) Store Manager contacts Regional Manager: report generator fuel status, estimated remaining runtime, store revenue impact; (b) if generator fuel is running low (&lt; 25%): Store Manager arranges emergency fuel delivery or coordinates with neighboring store for fuel sharing; (c) if outage will exceed generator capacity (&gt; 6–8 hours): Store Manager considers early closure per abbreviated W5F procedure; cash secured in safe, POS shut down, building secured; (d) Regional Manager reports extended outage stores to VP Store Operations for pattern analysis
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task13" name="Power restoration protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Power restoration protocol: When utility power is restored: (a) Maintenance switches from generator to utility power (do NOT run both simultaneously — risk of backfeed); (b) generator cooldown period (5 min idle before shutdown per manufacturer spec); (c) IT systems restart sequence: (1) network switch and WiFi access point, (2) POS terminals boot and reconnect, (3) POS sync with central server — validates offline transaction queue, (4) handheld devices reconnect, (5) CCTV system verifies recording resumed; (d) Department Supervisors verify lighting and displays restored; (e) Maintenance logs outage event: start time, end time, duration, generator runtime, fuel consumed, any issues
Responsible (R): Maintenance / IT (via phone support)
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task14" name="Post-outage reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-outage reconciliation: (a) POS system processes offline transaction queue (W5G offline recovery procedure); (b) Store Manager reviews offline transaction report for completeness; (c) Finance: no manual journal entry required if POS sync completes successfully; (d) Maintenance logs generator runtime and fuel consumption for facility cost tracking (W111 utility management); (e) if any data discrepancies from offline POS period: Store Manager flags to IT helpdesk (W48) for investigation
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Maintenance
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W470_Task15" name="Monthly pattern reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly pattern reporting: Regional Manager aggregates outage reports from all stores in region: (a) total outage hours per store per month, (b) generator fuel cost per store per month, (c) revenue impact estimate (compare sales during outage hours to same day/hour historical average); (d) stores with chronic outage issues (&gt; 8 hours/month) flagged for capex investment (permanent generator, solar panels per W173, or redundant utility feed); (e) report submitted to VP Store Operations monthly
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W470_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W470_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W470_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W470_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W470_Assoc18" sourceRef="W470_Annotation17" targetRef="W470_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
