    <bpmn:process id="W_W471" name="W471. Store-Level Security Incident &amp; Police/Barangay Reporting Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Security incident at a store that requires law enforcement involvement or formal documentation: shoplifting apprehension, break-in/burglary, vandalism, customer altercation, employee theft discovery, vehicle break-in in parking area, armed robbery
Frequency: ~2–5 incidents per store per year requiring formal reporting; ~400–1,000 total incidents/year chain-wide
Volume: 1 incident per event; some stores in high-crime areas may have 1–2 incidents/month
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Security Guard, LPO, Regional Manager, Facilities Coordinator, HR, Legal, Finance (Insurance)
Source: workflow W471 — Store-Level Security Incident &amp; Police/Barangay Reporting Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W471_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W471_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W471_Lane2" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W471_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W471_Start4" name="Security incident at a store that requires law enforcement involvement or formal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task5" name="Incident classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Incident classification: Store Manager or Security Guard classifies the incident on first report: Category A — Criminal (requires police): (a) armed robbery, (b) burglary/break-in (after hours), (c) shoplifting with apprehension and suspect detention, (d) employee theft discovered (per W37 investigation), (e) assault or violent customer altercation, (f) vehicle break-in in parking lot with property damage; Category B — Community dispute (barangay): (a) non-violent customer altercation, (b) minor property damage dispute, (c) noise or nuisance complaint from neighboring establishment; Category C — Internal documentation only: (a) attempted shoplifting (suspect fled, not apprehended), (b) minor vandalism (&lt; PHP 5,000 damage), (c) false alarm activation
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task6" name="Immediate response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Immediate response: (a) Category A: Security Guard secures the scene; if suspect detained, held in store office with CCTV coverage — do not use physical restraint beyond minimum necessary; Store Manager contacts PNP station immediately; if violence or weapon involved, staff safety is priority — do not confront; (b) Category B: Security Guard separates parties; Store Manager attempts de-escalation; if parties cannot resolve, proceed to barangay reporting; (c) Category C: Store Manager documents incident for internal records; LPO includes in daily exception report (W37)
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task7" name="Evidence preservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Evidence preservation: (a) Security Guard ensures CCTV recording of the incident is preserved — marks footage with timestamp, camera ID, and incident description; (b) if physical evidence exists (stolen merchandise recovered, damaged property, weapon), photographed in place before moved; (c) Store Manager identifies and separates witnesses (staff and customers); (d) for employee theft cases: do not tip off the employee until LPO is consulted per W37 investigation protocol; (e) all physical evidence tagged and stored in secure location (store manager&#x27;s office)
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task8" name="Police report filing (Category A)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Police report filing (Category A): (a) Store Manager or designated Security Guard goes to the nearest PNP station to file an incident report (commonly called &quot;blotter entry&quot; at PNP); (b) bring: Store Manager&#x27;s ID, store business permit (W54), CCTV footage on USB (selected clips only — do not provide full recording without formal request), recovered merchandise/evidence (if applicable), list of witnesses with contact information; (c) PNP officer records the incident in the police blotter — Store Manager requests a copy of the blotter entry (signed and stamped by investigating officer); (d) if suspect is detained: PNP takes custody of suspect and processes per Philippine criminal procedure; BuildRight staff should not detain suspects beyond reasonable time (~30 min max before PNP arrival)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task9" name="Barangay blotter entry (Category B)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Barangay blotter entry (Category B): (a) Store Manager or Security Guard goes to the barangay hall to file a blotter entry for community disputes; (b) barangay tanod records the incident; Store Manager requests a certified copy of the blotter entry; (c) barangay may schedule a conciliation meeting (Katarungang Pambarangay) — mandatory first step for minor disputes before court filing; (d) Store Manager attends conciliation meeting with documentation; settlement recorded by barangay
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min–1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task10" name="Insurance claim initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Insurance claim initiation (if property damage, theft, or robbery): (a) for incidents with estimated loss &gt; PHP 10,000: Store Manager notifies Facilities Coordinator and Finance (Treasury) within 24 hours; (b) Finance initiates insurance claim per W59 (Insurance Policy Lifecycle Management) — requires police report copy, photos, inventory loss valuation, and CCTV footage; (c) for robbery or burglary: insurance adjuster may visit the store for inspection — Store Manager coordinates access and preserves the scene until adjuster arrives (if practical)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min + insurance process</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task11" name="LP investigation handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: LP investigation handoff: Store Manager provides all incident documentation to LPO within 24 hours: (a) police/barangay blotter copy, (b) CCTV footage reference (camera ID and timestamp range), (c) witness contact list, (d) physical evidence inventory, (e) incident narrative; LPO incorporates into loss prevention investigation per W37 and enters into investigation case management (W37.10)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): LPO / Internal Audit
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task12" name="Employee-related incidents">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Employee-related incidents (if employee involvement): (a) for employee theft or fraud: HR is notified per W37 investigation protocol; employee placed on preventive suspension per Philippine Labor Code (due process); (b) for employee injury during incident: HR initiates incident report per W140 (OHS Incident Management) and coordinates with SSS for emergency medical benefit; (c) for employee as witness: HR documents witness statement; employee&#x27;s shift is adjusted for police/barangay attendance; (d) all employee-related actions comply with DOLE due process requirements — consult HR before any disciplinary action
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HR
Accountable (A): HR Head
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W471_Task13" name="Incident closure and reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Incident closure and reporting: (a) Store Manager closes incident in store incident register with: final classification, police/barangay report reference number, evidence disposition, estimated loss value, insurance claim status (if applicable), employee action (if applicable); (b) Monthly: Store Manager includes security incident summary in monthly store performance review (W67) — count by category, loss value, police/barangay report references; (c) Quarterly: Regional Manager aggregates security incident data across stores; identifies high-incident locations for LP intervention (increased patrols per W171, CCTV upgrades per W207, guard force changes); (d) Annual: LPO includes security incident trends in annual shrinkage report (W37.7)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations / Internal Audit
Duration: 15 min/case + monthly aggregation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W471_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W471_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W471_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W471_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W471_Assoc16" sourceRef="W471_Annotation15" targetRef="W471_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
