    <bpmn:process id="W_W497" name="W497. PWD Accessibility Compliance &amp; Store Facilities Audit" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual store facilities audit cycle; new store opening (W16); store renovation (W96); customer PWD complaint; DOLE/NCDA inspection advisory
Frequency: Annual (comprehensive audit); event-driven (complaint-triggered or new store)
Volume: 200 stores; annual audit of all locations; event-driven audits as needed
Owner: Store Operations — Facilities Standards Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Engineering &amp; Construction (W223), VP Store Operations, VP Legal, NCDA (National Council on Disability Affairs)
Source: workflow W497 — PWD Accessibility Compliance &amp; Store Facilities Audit</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W497_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W497_Lane1" name="Facilities Standards Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W497_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W497_Lane3" name="HR Training">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W497_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W497_Start5" name="Annual store facilities audit cycle; new store opening (W16); store renovation (W96)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task6" name="Accessibility Standards Checklist Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Accessibility Standards Checklist Preparation: Facilities Standards Manager maintains the PWD Accessibility Standards Checklist aligned with BP 344 and RA 7277 implementing rules: (a) Parking: designated PWD spaces per lot size, signage, pavement markings, ramp from parking to entrance; (b) Entrance: ramp gradient (max 1:12), handrails, level threshold, automatic or easy-open doors; (c) Pathways: minimum 1.2m aisle clearance throughout store, no protruding obstacles above 0.7m height, slip-resistant flooring; (d) Checkout: at least one lowered counter (max 0.8m height), accessible queue lane; (e) Restroom: at least one accessible toilet (wider door, grab bars, lowered sink, emergency call button); (f) Signage: PWD-accessible route signage, tactile floor indicators for blind customers at key decision points; (g) Service counter: at least one lowered section at customer service counter; (h) Emergency egress: accessible evacuation route, visual fire alarms (for hearing-impaired), designated assembly point accessible by ramp
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2 days/annual update</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task7" name="Annual Store Accessibility Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Annual Store Accessibility Audit: Facilities Standards Manager conducts annual audit of all 200 stores (can be delegated to Regional Managers with standardized checklist): (a) physical inspection of each store against checklist; (b) photograph and document non-compliance items; (c) rate each store: Compliant (all mandatory items met), Minor Non-Compliance (remediable within 30 days, no immediate safety risk), Major Non-Compliance (requires capital improvement, potential safety risk, or regulatory citation risk); (d) compile audit results into Store Accessibility Compliance Dashboard
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Mgr / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 hours/store × 200 stores = ~400–600 hours total (spread across team)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task8" name="New Store Accessibility Design Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: New Store Accessibility Design Review: During new store design (W223): (a) Engineering &amp; Construction incorporates PWD accessibility into store design standards; (b) Facilities Standards Manager reviews design plans for BP 344 compliance before construction; (c) verify accessibility in store layout planogram (W314) — aisle widths, checkout counter placement; (d) commissioning inspection (W227) includes accessibility verification; (e) obtain LGU building permit clearance for accessibility compliance (W54)
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Mgr / Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per W223</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task9" name="Minor Non-Compliance Remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Minor Non-Compliance Remediation: For stores with minor non-compliance: (a) Store Manager initiates corrective action within 30 days: clear obstructed pathways, install missing signage, adjust counter heights (if feasible without construction), re-stripe PWD parking spaces; (b) Facilities Standards Manager verifies remediation completion; (c) update compliance dashboard
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–30 days/item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task10" name="Major Non-Compliance Capital Remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Major Non-Compliance Capital Remediation: For stores with major non-compliance requiring construction: (a) Facilities Standards Manager submits capital improvement request (W21 — capex request); (b) scope: ramp installation, restroom modification, elevator/lift installation, parking lot reconfiguration; (c) Engineering &amp; Construction manages remediation project (W226 — store renovation); (d) target: complete within 6–12 months; prioritize by regulatory citation risk and customer complaint history
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Mgr / Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations / CFO
Duration: Per W21/W226</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task11" name="Customer Complaint Response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer Complaint Response: If a PWD customer files a complaint (W41) regarding accessibility: (a) Customer Service logs complaint with accessibility tag; (b) Facilities Standards Manager investigates complaint at the specific store; (c) assess whether complaint reveals non-compliance; (d) if non-compliance confirmed: initiate remediation (W497.4 or W497.5); (e) respond to customer with corrective action timeline; (f) if complaint escalates to DTI (W469) or NCDA: coordinate with VP Legal for regulatory response
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Mgr / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Per W41/W469</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task12" name="Staff Training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Staff Training: Store staff receive accessibility awareness training: (a) include PWD customer service module in new hire orientation (W15); (b) annual refresher: proper interaction with PWD customers, awareness of accessibility features in store, how to assist PWD customers with merchandise; (c) include in Store Manager training (W51) on accessibility compliance obligations and LGU inspection readiness
Responsible (R): HR Training (W51) / Facilities Standards Mgr
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per W15/W51</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W497_Task13" name="Regulatory Inspection Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Regulatory Inspection Coordination: If NCDA, DOLE, or LGU conducts a PWD accessibility inspection: (a) Facilities Standards Manager coordinates with Store Manager for inspection preparation; (b) provide accessibility audit reports and remediation evidence; (c) Store Manager hosts inspection visit; (d) Facilities Standards Manager coordinates response to any inspection findings; (e) archive inspection results in document management (W255) and compliance dashboard
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Mgr / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W497_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W497_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W497_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W497_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: corrective action orders
Owner: Store Operations — Facilities Standards Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W497_Assoc16" sourceRef="W497_Annotation15" targetRef="W497_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W497_Flow17" sourceRef="W497_Start5" targetRef="W497_Task6" />
