    <bpmn:process id="W_W559" name="W559. Store-Level Non-Emergency Incident &amp; Hazard Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer or employee reports non-emergency incident (minor slip, product spill, tripping hazard, property damage, broken fixture, parking lot issue)
Frequency: ~400–600 incidents per month across 200 stores (~2–3 per store per month)
Volume: Higher during rainy season (June–August, slip-and-fall), holiday peak (November–December, crowd incidents)
Owner: Store Manager / Safety Officer (Department Supervisor as delegate)
Participants: Reporting Person, Department Supervisor, Store Manager, Safety Officer (C), LP Officer (I), HR (I for employee incidents)
Source: workflow W559 — Store-Level Non-Emergency Incident &amp; Hazard Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W559_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W559_Lane1" name="Reporting Person">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W559_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W559_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W559_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W559_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W559_Start6" name="Customer or employee reports non-emergency incident (minor slip, product spill, tripping…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task7" name="Incident/hazard observed or reported">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Incident/hazard observed or reported: customer reports incident to nearest employee (e.g., &quot;I slipped on a wet floor in aisle 3&quot;); employee reports hazard during routine walk (e.g., Stock Associate notices water leak from ceiling); or LP Officer observes during daily routine (W562); reporting person notifies Department Supervisor immediately via radio or in person
Responsible (R): Reporting Person / Employee
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task8" name="Department Supervisor secures the area">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Department Supervisor secures the area: Supervisor immediately proceeds to location; places safety cone/barrier or &quot;Wet Floor&quot; sign to prevent further incidents; for spills: uses absorbent material from spill kit; for falling hazards (loose ceiling tile, unstable display): cordons off area with caution tape; assigns employee to stand guard if area cannot be physically blocked; ensures no customers or staff enter hazard zone
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task9" name="Supervisor documents incident on mobile form">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Supervisor documents incident on mobile form: Supervisor opens Incident Report form on handheld/tablet: (a) date/time (auto-populated), (b) store ID and location within store (aisle, department, yard, parking lot — selected from dropdown), (c) nature of incident (dropdown: slip/trip/fall, product spill, falling object, equipment malfunction, property damage, safety hazard, near-miss, other), (d) persons involved (name, contact info, customer vs. employee), (e) witness names and contact info, (f) narrative description (free text), (g) photo capture (minimum 2 photos: overview of scene + close-up of hazard/damage); form auto-saves as draft
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task10" name="For customer incidents — offer assistance and document">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For customer incidents — offer assistance and document: if incident involves a customer: (a) offer immediate assistance (&quot;Are you okay? Can I get you water/a chair?&quot;), (b) if customer appears injured — activate W501 first aid protocol (do NOT attempt to provide first aid beyond basic comfort unless certified first-aider), (c) if customer declines medical attention: document customer statement (&quot;Customer states they are not injured and decline medical attention&quot;), (d) provide incident report number for customer&#x27;s records, (e) offer to contact family member if needed, (f) do NOT admit liability or say &quot;it&#x27;s our fault&quot; — use neutral language (&quot;We&#x27;re sorry this happened; let me help you&quot;)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task11" name="For hazards — assess severity and remediate or schedule maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For hazards — assess severity and remediate or schedule maintenance: Supervisor assesses hazard severity: (a) Immediate risk to safety (e.g., exposed electrical wiring, structural damage) → remediate immediately or close area; (b) Moderate risk (e.g., loose tile, water leak, broken shelf) → schedule maintenance work order via W47 with target completion within 24 hours; (c) Low risk (e.g., minor cosmetic damage, faded signage) → schedule maintenance per normal W47 queue; for all hazard levels: hazard remains secured/barriered until remediation complete
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–5 min (assessment)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task12" name="For property damage — document and determine liability">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: For property damage — document and determine liability: if incident involves property damage (customer dropped and broke merchandise, forklift damaged shelf unit, vehicle hit parking lot barrier): (a) photograph damage from multiple angles, (b) estimate replacement/repair cost using system price lookup, (c) determine liability: customer-caused (customer offered option to pay for damage), store-caused (standard maintenance), third-party (vendor, contractor — refer to vendor agreement), (d) document liability determination in incident report
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W559_Task13" name="Submit incident report in ERP">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Submit incident report in ERP: Supervisor completes and submits incident report form; system auto-classifies into category: (a) Customer Incident — Injury, (b) Customer Incident — No Injury, (c) Employee Incident, (d) Property Damage, (e) Safety Hazard, (f) Near-Miss, (g) Parking Lot / Exterior; system assigns unique incident ID; incident record stored in store-level incident database; notification pushed to Store Manager for review
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W559_Task14" name="Store Manager reviews and classifies severity">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Store Manager reviews and classifies severity: Store Manager reviews submitted incident report; classifies severity: (a) Minor — no injury, minor property damage &lt; PHP 5,000, hazard easily remediated; (b) Moderate — minor injury treated on-site (W501), property damage PHP 5,000–50,000, hazard requiring maintenance work order; (c) Major — injury requiring off-site medical attention, property damage &gt; PHP 50,000, structural hazard, repeat incident at same location; Store Manager adds review notes and severity classification
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W559_Task15" name="Moderate/Major incidents forwarded to Regional LP and Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Moderate/Major incidents forwarded to Regional LP and Safety Officer: for Moderate and Major classifications: (a) system auto-notifies Regional LP Officer and Regional Safety Officer via email and push notification, (b) incident report with photos available in their dashboard, (c) Regional Safety Officer reviews within 24 hours for Major and 72 hours for Moderate, (d) if incident involves employee injury: HR notified automatically for DOLE reporting assessment (per W140 threshold), (e) if incident may result in liability claim: LP Officer flags for W285 public liability claims pre-registration
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Safety Officer / LP Officer
Duration: Notification: automated; Review: 15–30 min per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W559_Task16" name="System generates corrective action task if maintenance needed">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: System generates corrective action task if maintenance needed: if incident requires facility maintenance: (a) system auto-generates work order in Oracle eAM (W47, fit-gap F5), (b) work order linked to incident ID for traceability, (c) priority set based on incident severity (Major = emergency maintenance, Moderate = 24-hour SLA, Minor = normal queue), (d) maintenance completion updates incident record status; for recurring incidents at same location: system flags pattern for Root Cause Analysis assignment
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W559_Task17" name="Monthly incident summary report by store and category">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Monthly incident summary report by store and category: system generates monthly summary: (a) total incidents by store, (b) breakdown by category and severity, (c) top 10 stores by incident count, (d) repeat incident locations (same aisle/area flagged 2+ times), (e) average time-to-remediation for hazard-related incidents, (f) comparison to prior month and same month prior year; report distributed to Store Manager, Regional Manager, Safety Officer, and LP team
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (monthly batch report)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W559_Task18" name="Trend analysis feeding into preventive programs">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Trend analysis feeding into preventive programs: incident data feeds into: (a) W503 pest control and sanitation — spill pattern analysis for sanitation frequency adjustment, (b) W47 facility maintenance — recurring maintenance issues for capital improvement planning, (c) W140 OHS — employee incident trend for safety program improvement, (d) W285 liability claims — incident-to-claim conversion rate for insurance assessment, (e) Store performance scorecard (W67) — incident count as safety KPI; quarterly trend review by Regional Safety Officer
Responsible (R): System / Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Regional Safety Officer
Duration: Quarterly review: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W559_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W559_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W559_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W559_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: streamlined mobile form with photo-first design and dropdown-heavy (minimal typing) interface; operational: SLA tracking and escalation for overdue work orders; operational: classification guidelines with examples distributed quarterly and calibration sessions during Regional Manager meetings
Owner: Store Manager / Safety Officer (Department Supervisor as delegate)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
