    <bpmn:process id="W_W576" name="W576. Store-Level Typhoon &amp; Severe Weather Preparedness Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA issues tropical cyclone advisory (TCWS Signal 1 or higher) for any store location
Frequency: ~20 typhoon events/year affecting the Philippine archipelago (PAGASA average of ~20 tropical cyclones entering the PAR, ~8–9 making landfall); individual store impact varies
Volume: During typhoon season (June–November), average 20–40 stores affected per event (Signal 1); Signal 2–3 events may affect 60–100 stores; major events (Signal 4–5) may affect 100+ stores simultaneously (per the W1302 signal-tier scale)
Owner: VP Store Operations (HQ activation); Store Manager (store-level execution)
Participants: VP Store Operations, Regional Managers, Store Managers, Safety Officer, Security, LP, Insurance, Facilities
Source: workflow W576 — Store-Level Typhoon &amp; Severe Weather Preparedness Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W576_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W576_Lane1" name="Store Ops Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W576_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W576_Lane3" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W576_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W576_Start5" name="PAGASA issues tropical cyclone advisory (TCWS Signal 1 or higher) for any store location">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task6" name="Pre-season preparation (April–May)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-season preparation (April–May): HQ distributes typhoon preparedness kits to all 200 stores (sandbags, tarps, emergency lighting, battery radio, first aid restock); Store Manager verifies kit completeness; generators tested per W111
Responsible (R): Store Ops Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2 weeks (annual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task7" name="PAGASA monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: PAGASA monitoring: HQ monitors PAGASA tropical cyclone bulletins every 6 hours during active weather disturbances; automated alerts pushed to Regional Managers and affected Store Managers when TCWS raised for any store province
Responsible (R): Store Ops Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Continuous during events</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task8" name="Signal 1 (Alert Mode)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Signal 1 (Alert Mode): affected stores execute: (a) secure all outdoor merchandise and display fixtures (yard, garden center), (b) test backup generator and verify fuel level, (c) activate staff contact tree — confirm all employees have emergency contact info, (d) increase cash holdings for potential multi-day offline operations per W580, (e) verify POS offline capability per W535 (full SKU catalog + customer cache current)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task9" name="Signal 2 (Reduced Operations)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Signal 2 (Reduced Operations): (a) Regional Manager authorizes early closure if conditions warrant, (b) expedite remaining customer transactions, (c) pre-position emergency supplies (flashlights, water, first aid), (d) cash safe reinforcement — all excess cash deposited per W541 before closure, (e) staff release plan communicated (essential staff only to remain for securing facility)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task10" name="Signal 3+ (Full Closure)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Signal 3+ (Full Closure): (a) complete customer evacuation per W330, (b) lock down facility — all doors, windows, dock doors secured, (c) sandbag entry points if flood risk, (d) activate alarm system despite closure, (e) all staff released except minimum security presence (1 guard with emergency communication), (f) Store Manager submits closure notification to HQ dashboard
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task11" name="During typhoon">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: During typhoon: HQ maintains real-time store status dashboard; affected Store Managers send hourly status updates (if communication available); Regional Manager monitors portfolio
Responsible (R): Store Ops Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task12" name="Post-typhoon damage assessment (within 24 hours of all-clear)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-typhoon damage assessment (within 24 hours of all-clear): Store Manager conducts damage assessment using standardized checklist: (a) structural damage (roof, walls, doors, windows), (b) flooding/water damage to inventory, (c) equipment damage, (d) electrical system status, (e) inventory loss estimate; photographs all damage; submits assessment to HQ
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task13" name="Insurance claim initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Insurance claim initiation: for stores with damage exceeding PHP 50K, HQ Insurance Coordinator initiates claim with insurer per W59; provides Store Manager&#x27;s damage assessment, photos, and inventory loss details
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 hours per claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W576_Task14" name="Reopening checklist">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Reopening checklist: (a) structural safety confirmed (no visible damage or damage repaired), (b) power restored or generator operational, (c) water supply confirmed, (d) POS connectivity verified (online sync with HQ per W533), (e) damaged inventory segregated and documented per W91, (f) staff safety confirmed (no employee injuries), (g) Store Manager submits reopening notification to HQ dashboard
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W576_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W576_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W576_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W576_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: satellite phone at each DC (fallback communication point) and pre-arranged SMS check-in protocol via backup carrier; operational: pre-positioning inventory above floor level during Signal 1, and flood insurance riders; operational: Signal 1 preparation completing all securing activities so minimal travel needed at higher signal levels
Owner: VP Store Operations (HQ activation); Store Manager (store-level execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W576_Assoc17" sourceRef="W576_Annotation16" targetRef="W576_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
