    <bpmn:process id="W_W582" name="W582. Store-Level Fire Drill Execution &amp; Documentation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled semi-annual fire drill; or unscheduled drill required by BFP after incident or inspection
Frequency: Semi-annual per store (2/year, matching the 400-drills/year Time Estimate; W330&#x27;s quarterly cadence covers the broader emergency-drill program)
Volume: 200 stores × 2 drills/year = 400 drills/year; each drill involves all staff on duty (~29 employees per store)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: All Store Staff on duty, any customers present, Safety Officer (HQ advisory)
Source: workflow W582 — Store-Level Fire Drill Execution &amp; Documentation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W582_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W582_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W582_Lane2" name="Fire Warden">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W582_Lane3" name="All Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W582_Lane4" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W582_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W582_Start6" name="Scheduled semi-annual fire drill; or unscheduled drill required by BFP after incident or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task7" name="Drill scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Drill scheduling (T-1 week): Store Manager schedules drill date with Regional Manager approval; select off-peak hours (typically 2:00–3:00 PM weekday or 9:00–10:00 AM weekend); alternate morning/afternoon between drills; notify BFP local fire station if required by local ordinance
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task8" name="Staff briefing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Staff briefing (T-1 day): brief all staff on evacuation routes, assembly point location, fire wardens per zone, and drill procedures; do NOT announce exact drill time to maintain realistic response
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task9" name="Drill day — activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Drill day — activation: designated fire warden activates fire alarm; timer starts
Responsible (R): Fire Warden
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task10" name="Evacuation execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Evacuation execution: (a) Sales Associates guide customers to nearest exit; priority: customers near fire hazards (paint, chemicals, lumber), (b) Cashiers secure cash drawers (close and lock), (c) Stock Associates in backroom/receiving dock evacuate via designated rear exits, (d) Fire wardens sweep assigned zones to verify complete evacuation (check restrooms, break room, fitting areas), (e) Store Manager or designee checks for anyone requiring assistance (PWD, elderly)
Responsible (R): All Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–5 min (target)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task11" name="Assembly point accountability">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Assembly point accountability: all staff report to designated assembly point (outside building, minimum 50m from structure); Department Supervisors conduct biometric/roll call verification against staff on-duty roster; note any missing persons
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task12" name="All-clear signal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: All-clear signal: Store Manager confirms all persons accounted for; announces all-clear and directs orderly building re-entry
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task13" name="Post-drill debrief">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-drill debrief (within 30 min of drill): (a) evacuation time vs. target (&lt; 5 minutes), (b) issues identified (blocked exits, confused staff, missing persons, customer resistance), (c) corrective actions with owners and deadlines, (d) staff questions and feedback
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Safety Officer
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task14" name="BFP-compliant documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: BFP-compliant documentation: complete fire drill report form: (a) drill date and time, (b) number of participants (staff + estimated customers), (c) evacuation time, (d) issues and corrective actions, (e) fire warden names, (f) assembly point confirmation, (g) Store Manager signature; file in store records and submit copy to Safety Officer (HQ) for BFP FSIC compliance per W476
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Safety Officer
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W582_Task15" name="Corrective action tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Corrective action tracking: any issues identified during drill are entered as corrective actions in system; tracked to completion before next drill; unresolved corrective actions escalated to Regional Manager
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W582_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W582_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W582_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W582_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: clear PA announcement &quot;This is a fire drill — please follow staff to exits&quot; and staff training to firmly but politely escort customers; operational: separate yard evacuation procedure and designated outdoor assembly point away from vehicle traffic; operational: standardized BFP-compliant template and HQ Safety Officer review of all drill reports
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W582_Assoc18" sourceRef="W582_Annotation17" targetRef="W582_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
