    <bpmn:process id="W_W774" name="W774. Store-Level Parking Lot &amp; Exterior Facility Daily Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of each store business day; and ad-hoc incident response
Frequency: Daily; continuous during business hours
Volume: 200 stores × daily exterior facility management
Owner: Maintenance / Utility Staff
Participants: Maintenance Staff, Store Manager, Security Guard
Source: workflow W774 — Store-Level Parking Lot &amp; Exterior Facility Daily Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W774_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W774_Lane1" name="Maintenance Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W774_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W774_Start3" name="Start of each store business day; and ad-hoc incident response">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task4" name="Morning exterior walkthrough">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning exterior walkthrough: Maintenance Staff performs opening exterior inspection: (a) parking lot condition (potholes, debris, standing water from overnight rain), (b) signage lighting and visibility, (c) PWD parking space availability and markings per BP 344, (d) fire lane clearance per BFP requirements, (e) outdoor lumber yard security and inventory stacking, (f) garden center plant condition and watering needs
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task5" name="Parking lot preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Parking lot preparation: (a) remove any overnight debris, abandoned items, or hazards, (b) verify parking striping visibility, (c) check cart return corrals are empty and positioned, (d) confirm PWD ramp accessibility unobstructed, (e) verify exterior lighting operational for early morning/evening hours
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task6" name="Customer cart retrieval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer cart retrieval: Throughout the day: Maintenance Staff retrieves shopping carts from parking lot at regular intervals (every 30-60 minutes during peak, every 2 hours off-peak); returns to store entrance; verifies cart condition (broken wheels, clean)
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/trip, ~8–12 trips/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task7" name="Mid-day exterior check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Mid-day exterior check: (a) parking lot capacity observation (overflow triggers notification to Store Manager for potential traffic management), (b) exterior signage still operational, (c) outdoor display areas (garden center, lumber promotional displays) maintained, (d) loading bay area clear and organized per W723
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task8" name="Hazard response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Hazard response: For exterior hazards during business hours: (a) oil/chemical spill in parking lot — contain and clean per hazmat procedure W238, (b) broken glass — immediate cleanup, (c) flooding from heavy rain — deploy warning signs and sandbags, (d) fallen tree/branch — clear pathway and file maintenance work order per W47
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10-30 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task9" name="End-of-day exterior close">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: End-of-day exterior close: (a) final cart retrieval from parking lot, (b) exterior lighting check (parking lot lights on for safety), (c) garden center items that need overnight protection moved indoors or covered, (d) outdoor lumber yard secured, (e) parking lot gate/closure (if applicable)
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W774_Task10" name="Weekly exterior maintenance checklist">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Weekly exterior maintenance checklist: Weekly: (a) parking lot line striping assessment, (b) exterior signage cleaning, (c) PWD ramp and accessible path condition check per W497, (d) gutter and drainage clearing (Philippine rainy season critical), (e) exterior paint and facade condition assessment
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W774_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W774_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W774_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W774_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Maintenance / Utility Staff</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W774_Assoc13" sourceRef="W774_Annotation12" targetRef="W774_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
