    <bpmn:process id="W_W1005" name="W1005. Store-Level Shelf Stock Rotation &amp; Paint/Chemical Expiry Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily scheduled task; also triggered by new batch receipt and product expiry alert
Frequency: Daily per store, focused on paint, adhesives, sealants, chemicals, and consumables
Volume: ~800–1,200 SKUs monitored per store (paint, chemical, adhesive, consumable categories)
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Finishes)
Participants: Sales Associate (Stock Associate rotation), Category Manager (expiry policy)
Source: workflow W1005 — Store-Level Shelf Stock Rotation &amp; Paint/Chemical Expiry Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1005_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1005_Lane1" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1005_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1005_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1005_Start4" name="Daily scheduled task; also triggered by new batch receipt and product expiry alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1005_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1005_Task5" name="Daily FIFO Shelf Rotation Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily FIFO Shelf Rotation Check: Stock Associate walks assigned aisles (paint, adhesives, sealants, chemicals); for each SKU batch on shelf: (a) check batch/lot date label (arrival date sticker applied at receiving per W109); (b) verify older stock is positioned in front of newer stock; (c) re-arrange any out-of-sequence batches to ensure FIFO compliance; (d) scan shelf barcode with RF gun to confirm rotation check completion; (e) system logs rotation check with timestamp and associate ID
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1005_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1005_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1005_Task6" name="Expiry Date Scan &amp; Alert Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Expiry Date Scan &amp; Alert Processing: Stock Associate uses RF gun to scan batch/lot barcodes of all monitored SKUs; system compares batch date against shelf life master data per SKU: (a) Green (&gt; 6 months to expiry): no action; (b) Amber (3–6 months to expiry): system generates markdown recommendation per W93 — progressive markdown: 10% at 6 months, 20% at 4 months, 30% at 3 months; markdown applied by Category Manager approval; (c) Red (&lt; 3 months to expiry): system flags for priority clearance — 40–50% markdown, bundle with compatible products, or return to vendor per W88 if vendor has return agreement; (d) Expired: immediate shelf removal, quarantine in backroom hazmat area, disposition per W91 (damaged/defective goods)
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–25 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1005_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1005_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1005_Task7" name="Approaching-Expiry Markdown Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Approaching-Expiry Markdown Execution: For Amber/Red items: (a) Department Supervisor reviews system-generated markdown recommendations; (b) applies markdown per authority matrix (up to 20% markdown: Supervisor approval; 20–40%: Store Manager approval; &gt;40%: Category Manager approval); (c) system updates POS price file and shelf label per W181; (d) new price labels printed and applied to shelf; (e) if ecommerce-eligible, markdown reflected on buildright.com.ph per ECOM-002; (f) markdown tracked per SKU for margin impact analysis
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1005_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1005_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1005_Task8" name="Expired Product Quarantine &amp; Disposal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Expired Product Quarantine &amp; Disposal: For expired items: (a) Stock Associate removes from shelf and places in quarantine bin in backroom; (b) scan-out from active inventory with &quot;expired&quot; disposition code per W91; (c) system creates disposal request for Department Supervisor approval; (d) hazardous expired products (solvents, chemicals) stored per W236 and collected by DENR-accredited transporter per W82; (e) non-hazardous expired products disposed per store waste management (W502); (f) inventory write-off posted to GL with expiry loss account; (g) monthly expiry loss report generated for Category Manager review and supplier quality follow-up
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1005_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1005_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1005_Task9" name="Supplier Quality Feedback Loop">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Supplier Quality Feedback Loop: Monthly: (a) Department Supervisor compiles store-level expiry and quality issue summary by SKU and vendor; (b) report submitted to Category Manager; (c) recurring expiry issues (same SKU expiring within 6 months of receipt) indicate supplier sending aged stock or shelf life master data needs correction; (d) Category Manager escalates to vendor per W110 (Supplier Quality &amp; CAPA) and W44 (Vendor Performance Review); (e) if vendor consistently sends short-dated stock, Buyer renegotiates delivery terms or evaluates alternative supplier per W631 (Strategic Sourcing)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Monthly: 30–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1005_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1005_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1005_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1005_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1005_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Finishes) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Finishes)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1005_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1005_Annotation11" targetRef="W1005_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1005_Flow13" sourceRef="W1005_Start4" targetRef="W1005_Task5" />
