    <bpmn:process id="W_W1023" name="W1023. Store-Level Post-Typhoon Damage Assessment, Cleanup &amp; Rapid Reopening" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA typhoon signal lifted for store area; or store manager declares safe to assess after severe weather event
Frequency: ~5–10 events/year affecting subsets of the 200-store chain (Philippines averages 20 typhoons/year; any given store is affected 1–3 times/year)
Volume: 1 assessment per store per event; 10–50 stores affected per major typhoon
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Assistant Store Manager, Department Supervisors, Maintenance/Utility Staff, Regional Operations Manager, Insurance Claims Coordinator, LP Officer
Source: workflow W1023 — Store-Level Post-Typhoon Damage Assessment, Cleanup &amp; Rapid Reopening</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1023_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1023_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1023_Lane2" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1023_Lane3" name="All Store Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1023_Lane4" name="Regional Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1023_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1023_Start6" name="PAGASA typhoon signal lifted for store area; or store manager declares safe to assess…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1023_Task7" name="Initial Safety Assessment &amp; Facility Clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Initial Safety Assessment &amp; Facility Clearance: After PAGASA signal lift, Store Manager and Maintenance/Utility Staff conduct exterior and interior walkthrough: (a) check structural integrity — roof, walls, columns, ceiling, outdoor yard canopy; (b) check electrical system — no downed power lines, no standing water near electrical panels, main breaker status; (c) check for flooding — standing water depth in selling floor, backroom, and yard; (d) check for fallen trees, debris blocking entrance/exit and loading dock; (e) document all damage with timestamped photos (minimum 30 photos: exterior 4 sides, roof, interior each department, backroom, yard, electrical room); (f) if any structural or electrical hazard found, building is unsafe — do not enter; secure perimeter and contact Regional Operations Manager for engineering assessment per W789; (g) if building is safe, proceed to step 2
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1023_Task8" name="Inventory Damage Assessment &amp; Quarantine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inventory Damage Assessment &amp; Quarantine: Department Supervisors assess inventory damage in their respective areas: (a) water-damaged items: cement (hardened bags), gypsum board (swollen/warped), plywood/lumber (warped, delaminated), electrical wire/cable (water ingress compromises insulation safety), adhesives/sealants (label damage, water-contaminated contents), paint (rusted cans, label destroyed); (b) physically damaged items: broken tiles, shattered glass, crushed packaging from fallen shelving or debris; (c) scan all damaged items with RF gun using &quot;typhoon damage&quot; disposition code; system segregates damaged inventory from available stock in real-time; (d) move damaged items to designated quarantine area in backroom; (e) system generates damage report with SKU, quantity, cost value, and retail value; (f) water-sensitive items (cement, adhesives, MDF/gypsum) that appear undamaged but were exposed to moisture are tagged for 48-hour observation before clearance
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors / Stock Associates
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 60–120 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1023_Task9" name="Cleanup &amp; Sanitation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cleanup &amp; Sanitation: All available store staff execute cleanup: (a) remove debris, fallen signage, broken glass, and fallen inventory from aisles; (b) pump out standing water (portable submersible pump from backroom emergency supplies); (c) dry wet surfaces — mops, wet vacuums, and fans deployed; (d) sanitize all surfaces that contacted flood water (contamination risk); (e) inspect and clean all POS terminals, card readers, and customer-facing displays; (f) clear parking lot, entrance, and loading dock of debris; (g) restore planogram compliance — re-shelf displaced inventory per W573; (h) verify fire extinguishers, emergency exits, and safety equipment are intact and accessible per W758
Responsible (R): All Store Staff
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1023_Task10" name="Insurance Claim Documentation &amp; Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Insurance Claim Documentation &amp; Reporting: Store Manager compiles damage documentation package: (a) structural damage assessment with photos sent to Regional Operations Manager and Engineering team per W789; (b) inventory damage report from system (step 2) with cost and retail value totals; (c) equipment damage assessment (POS terminals, RF guns, forklift, paint mixing station per W1003); (d) business interruption impact estimate (days/hours closed, estimated lost revenue); (e) complete package uploaded to insurance claims module per W858 (typhoon/natural disaster insurance claim); (f) for losses exceeding PHP 500,000 per store, Insurance Claims Coordinator contacts insurance adjuster for on-site inspection scheduling; (g) system generates GL entries for inventory write-off (W92) and fixed asset impairment (W39)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Insurance Claims Coordinator
Accountable (A): Regional Operations Manager
Duration: 45–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1023_Task11" name="Reopening Decision &amp; Demand Surge Replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reopening Decision &amp; Demand Surge Replenishment: Regional Operations Manager and Store Manager make reopening decision: (a) reopening criteria: building structurally safe, electrical system operational, all aisles clear and safe for customer traffic, fire safety equipment functional, minimum 1 POS terminal operational; (b) if criteria met, store reopens — Store Manager activates &quot;reopening&quot; status in system; (c) system triggers automatic emergency replenishment order per W927 for high-demand post-typhoon items: plywood (4×8 sheets), GI roofing sheets, nails (common wire nails, roofing nails), tarps/tarpaulins, waterproofing sealant, electrical wire, PVC pipes and fittings, hammer and saw sets, cement (if available); (d) replenishment order flagged as priority in DC dispatch per W106; (e) if store cannot reopen (structural damage), coordinate temporary operations: limited outdoor sale of non-damaged inventory from parking lot (with LGU permit per W446) or redirect customers to nearest open store per system real-time inventory check
Responsible (R): Regional Operations Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1023_Task12" name="Post-Recovery Customer Communication &amp; Community Support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-Recovery Customer Communication &amp; Community Support: (a) system sends SMS/push notification to loyalty members in store&#x27;s trade area: &quot;BuildRight [Store Name] is OPEN. Post-typhoon rebuild materials available — plywood, roofing, nails, tarps, waterproofing. Trade account holders: priority loading available&quot;; (b) activate post-disaster community assistance per W428 (community disaster relief); (c) offer contractor referral service per W904 for customers needing professional rebuild help; (d) for severely affected areas, coordinate with local government and DTI for price freeze compliance per W468 (RA 7581 price control); (e) Store Manager submits post-event report to Regional Operations Manager within 48 hours: damage summary, recovery timeline, sales recovery trajectory, lessons learned
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Marketing Team
Accountable (A): Regional Operations Manager
Duration: 30–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1023_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1023_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1023_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1023_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1023_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1023_Annotation14" targetRef="W1023_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow16" sourceRef="W1023_Start6" targetRef="W1023_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow17" sourceRef="W1023_Task7" targetRef="W1023_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow18" sourceRef="W1023_Task8" targetRef="W1023_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow19" sourceRef="W1023_Task9" targetRef="W1023_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow20" sourceRef="W1023_Task10" targetRef="W1023_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow21" sourceRef="W1023_Task11" targetRef="W1023_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1023_Flow22" sourceRef="W1023_Task12" targetRef="W1023_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1023_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1023_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1023">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1023_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1023_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
