    <bpmn:process id="W_W1040" name="W1040. Store-Level Customer Parking Lot Traffic Safety &amp; Exterior Facility Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily scheduled opening check; monthly safety inspection; incident-triggered response
Frequency: Daily visual check; monthly structured inspection; incident response as needed
Volume: 200 stores; each store has 80–150 parking spaces
Owner: Assistant Store Manager
Participants: Maintenance/Utility Staff, Security Guard, LP Officer, Customer Service Rep
Source: workflow W1040 — Store-Level Customer Parking Lot Traffic Safety &amp; Exterior Facility Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1040_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1040_Lane1" name="Maintenance Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1040_Lane2" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1040_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1040_Start4" name="Daily scheduled opening check; monthly safety inspection; incident-triggered response">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1040_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1040_Task5" name="Daily Parking Lot Opening Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily Parking Lot Opening Check: Before store opening, Maintenance/Utility Staff and Security Guard conduct check: (a) remove any debris, fallen branches, or standing water from parking lot; (b) verify parking lot lighting is operational (all fixtures illuminated during pre-dawn check for stores opening at 7 AM); (c) check parking lot surface for potholes, cracks, or raised sections — mark with safety cones or caution tape; (d) verify speed bumps and lane markings are visible; repaint faded markings monthly; (e) verify directional signage (entrance, exit, one-way arrows) is intact and visible; (f) verify PWD/elderly parking slots (minimum 2 per lot per BP 344 accessibility law) are clearly marked and unobstructed; (g) verify cart corrals are in designated positions and empty of carts (carts returned to store entrance per W1028); (h) verify loading dock area is separated from customer parking by physical barrier (bollards or chained area) — customer vehicles must not enter dock zone where forklifts operate per W1015; (i) verify BOPIS pickup area signage and designated spots are clear per W11
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1040_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1040_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1040_Task6" name="Traffic Flow &amp; Customer Loading Safety">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Traffic Flow &amp; Customer Loading Safety: During store hours: (a) Security Guard monitors parking lot traffic flow: enforce one-way traffic pattern, prevent customer vehicles from blocking dock area or fire lanes; (b) for customers loading bulky items (lumber, cement, appliances) onto personal vehicles: (i) Customer Service Rep or designated loading assistant (W950) helps customer move items from flatbed cart to vehicle using the designated customer loading zone adjacent to lumber yard exit; (ii) loading zone is a marked area separate from driving lanes — no loading in active traffic lanes; (iii) flatbed cart never left unattended in parking lot; returned to store immediately after loading per W1028; (c) during peak hours (Saturday 10AM–2PM, payday weekends): Security Guard stationed at entrance/exit to manage traffic flow, especially when delivery trucks are entering/exiting dock area simultaneously with customer traffic; (d) for BOPIS pickup: customer pulls into designated BOPIS spot, staff brings order to vehicle per W11 — no customer leaves vehicle in BOPIS zone
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: Continuous during store hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1040_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1040_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1040_Task7" name="Monthly Safety Inspection &amp; Maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly Safety Inspection &amp; Maintenance: Monthly: (a) Maintenance Staff and Assistant Store Manager conduct structured parking lot inspection: (i) Surface condition: inspect for potholes (&gt; 5 cm deep requires asphalt repair), cracks (&gt; 2 cm wide requires sealing), standing water areas (indicates drainage problem), and faded lane markings; (ii) Drainage: verify all drain grates are clear of debris; test drainage flow by running water — any pooling &gt; 2 cm depth for &gt; 30 minutes indicates blocked drain or grading problem; (iii) Lighting: measure illuminance at darkest points using lux meter — minimum 20 lux per Philippine building code for commercial parking; replace any burned-out fixtures within 48 hours; (iv) Signage: verify all traffic signs (stop, yield, speed limit 10 kph, PWD parking, BOPIS pickup, no parking zones) are visible, legible, and undamaged; (v) Safety equipment: fire extinguisher at charging station for electric vehicles (if applicable), first aid kit at entrance; (vi) Security: verify CCTV coverage of parking lot per W838 (minimum 4 cameras covering entrance, exit, dock area, and main lot); (b) maintenance work orders created per W47 for all identified issues with priority classification: urgent (safety hazard, fix within 24 hours), standard (fix within 2 weeks), planned (next scheduled maintenance)
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Assistant Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 60–90 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1040_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1040_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1040_Task8" name="Incident Response &amp; Customer Safety">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Incident Response &amp; Customer Safety: If a parking lot incident occurs (customer vehicle accident, customer slip/fall, theft, vehicle break-in): (a) Security Guard responds immediately: secure the area, check for injuries; (b) if injury: activate first aid response per W501 (First Aid &amp; Medical Emergency); call emergency services (911) if serious; (c) if vehicle accident: document with photos, provide witness statement forms, do not admit liability; (d) if theft/vehicle break-in: preserve CCTV footage per W838, assist customer in filing police report at nearest barangay station per W471; (e) if customer slip/fall due to surface hazard: document with photos of hazard, provide first aid, and report to Store Manager for incident documentation per W285 (Public Liability Claims); (f) all incidents logged in system with date, time, location (GPS), description, and resolution; (g) recurring incidents at same location trigger root cause analysis and corrective action (e.g., repainting of faded crosswalk after 3 near-miss incidents)
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per incident: 15–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1040_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1040_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1040_Task9" name="Seasonal Weather Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Seasonal Weather Preparation: Before rainy season (June) and typhoon season (July–November): (a) inspect and clean all drainage systems — remove accumulated debris from drain grates, clear drainage channels, and verify stormwater detention area (if applicable) is functional; (b) repair any parking lot surface damage that could worsen with rain (potholes fill with water, concealing depth); (c) verify emergency lighting (parking lot lights on generator backup per W808) — critical during typhoon-related power outages when customers may be in the parking lot; (d) stockpile sandbags at dock area entrance to prevent floodwater from entering building; (e) verify security lighting is functional — criminals exploit power outages during typhoons for vehicle break-ins
Responsible (R): Maintenance Staff / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours (seasonal prep)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1040_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1040_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1040_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1040_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1040_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: (numbered slots, estimated wait time display) reduces customer frustration
Owner: Assistant Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
