        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1047_Start5" name="Philippine rainy season onset (June–November, per PAGASA); or continuous rainfall for ≥2…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1047_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1047_Task6" name="Rainy Season Preparation (Annual Setup)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Rainy Season Preparation (Annual Setup): Before June 1 each year, Maintenance/Utility Staff executes annual rainy season readiness: (a) inspect and clean all entrance drainage channels — ensure grates are clear of debris and connected to storm drain; (b) inspect entrance canopy/overhang — no leaks, no accumulated debris on top, gutters clear; (c) inspect and deploy anti-slip floor mats at all entrance points — rubber-backed water-absorbent mats in good condition (replace if worn); (d) verify wet floor sign inventory — minimum 4 &quot;Wet Floor&quot; A-frame warning signs per entrance; (e) verify umbrella bag dispenser (at entrance) is stocked — prevents water dripping throughout store; (f) verify store entrance door seals and weatherstripping are intact; (g) test entrance area lighting — adequate visibility for wet floor hazard identification; (h) system logs rainy season readiness checklist completion with date and Store Manager sign-off
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 60–90 min (one-time annual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1047_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1047_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1047_Task7" name="Daily Rainy Day Activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily Rainy Day Activation: When rain begins (or at store opening if already raining): (a) Maintenance/Utility Staff deploys &quot;Wet Floor&quot; warning signs at all entrance points and at transition zones (entrance to main aisle); (b) lays out anti-slip floor mats at full width of each entrance (ensure mats lie flat, no curling edges); (c) positions umbrella bag dispenser at entrance — customer service representative reminds entering customers to use umbrella bags; (d) assigns a Sales Associate or Customer Service Rep as &quot;entrance monitor&quot; during peak hours (10 AM–2 PM, 4 PM–7 PM) to mop accumulated water and reposition mats as needed; (e) activates entrance canopy rain deflector (if automated) or manually adjusts canopy angle to direct runoff away from entrance; (f) system logs daily rainy day activation with timestamp
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff / Sales Associates
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min (per activation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1047_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1047_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1047_Task8" name="Continuous Wet Floor Management During Rain">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Continuous Wet Floor Management During Rain: Throughout the rainy period: (a) entrance monitor mops entrance area every 30 minutes during active rainfall; (b) checks and replaces saturated floor mats with dry spare mats (each store maintains 4 spare mats for rotation); (c) places additional &quot;Caution: Slippery Floor&quot; cone signs in areas with standing water; (d) monitors backroom receiving dock for water intrusion — goods receipt operations may need temporary suspension if dock is flooded per W109; (e) monitors outdoor lumber yard — cover exposed merchandise with tarps per W1010 (garden center weather protection procedures adapted for lumber yard); (f) LP Officer monitors CCTV entrance coverage per W838 for slip-and-fall incidents
Responsible (R): Entrance Monitor (rotating Sales Associate)
Accountable (A): Assistant Store Manager
Duration: Continuous during rain (30-min intervals)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1047_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1047_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1047_Task9" name="Post-Rain Cleanup &amp; Deactivation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-Rain Cleanup &amp; Deactivation: When rain stops and entrance area is dry: (a) remove &quot;Wet Floor&quot; signs; (b) collect and wash saturated floor mats — hang to dry in backroom; (c) replace with dry permanent mats; (d) mop and dry entrance floor completely; (e) check and restock umbrella bag dispenser; (f) inspect entrance area for any water damage to flooring or shelving near entrance; (g) system logs deactivation time and any incidents
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1047_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1047_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1047_Task10" name="Incident Response (If Slip-and-Fall Occurs)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Incident Response (If Slip-and-Fall Occurs): If a customer or employee slips: (a) LP Officer and Store Manager respond immediately per W140 (OHS incident management) and W285 (public liability claims); (b) administer first aid per W501 (first aid &amp; medical emergency response); (c) if injury requires medical attention: offer transport to nearest hospital/clinic, document incident per OHS protocol; (d) complete incident report: date, time, location, conditions, witness statements, CCTV footage preservation per W838; (e) photograph area conditions (mat status, signs, wetness level); (f) report to insurance coordinator per W863 (third-party liability claim); (g) if incident reveals systemic issue (inadequate mat, poor drainage), Store Manager initiates corrective action per W140; (h) system logs incident in OHS module with full documentation chain
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min (per incident)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1047_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1047_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1047_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1047_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1047_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: during rainy season
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1047_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1047_Annotation12" targetRef="W1047_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1047_Flow14" sourceRef="W1047_Start5" targetRef="W1047_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1047_Flow15" sourceRef="W1047_Task6" targetRef="W1047_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1047_Flow16" sourceRef="W1047_Task7" targetRef="W1047_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1047_Flow17" sourceRef="W1047_Task8" targetRef="W1047_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1047_Flow18" sourceRef="W1047_Task9" targetRef="W1047_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1047_Flow19" sourceRef="W1047_Task10" targetRef="W1047_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
