    <bpmn:process id="W_W1119" name="W1119. Store-Level Outdoor Garden Center Seasonal Plant Inventory Lifecycle" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal calendar trigger (W306), nursery supplier delivery schedule, or garden center daily operations
Frequency: Weekly (during peak season Mar–May); bi-weekly (off-season)
Volume: 50–150 live plant SKUs per store × 200 stores = 10,000–30,000 live plant inventory records
Owner: Department Supervisor (Garden &amp; Outdoor)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate (Garden Center), Stock Associate, Category Manager (Garden)
Source: workflow W1119 — Store-Level Outdoor Garden Center Seasonal Plant Inventory Lifecycle</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1119_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1119_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1119_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1119_Lane3" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1119_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1119_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1119_Start6" name="Seasonal calendar trigger (W306), nursery supplier delivery schedule, or garden center…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1119_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1119_Task7" name="Seasonal Plant Assortment Planning &amp; Ordering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal Plant Assortment Planning &amp; Ordering: (a) Category Manager defines seasonal plant assortment: (i) Dry/Summer (Mar–May): flowering annuals (zinnias, marigolds, cosmos), vegetables (tomato, chili pepper, eggplant seedlings), herbs (basil, mint, rosemary), lawn grass plugs; (ii) Rainy Season (Jun–Oct): hardy ornamentals (croton, bougainvillea, palm varieties), indoor plants (pothos, sansevieria, aglaonema), ground covers; (iii) Holiday (Nov–Dec): poinsettias, Christmas cactus, wreath materials; (iv) Year-round: succulents, cacti, orchids, bonsai; (b) Department Supervisor places order with local nursery supplier 1–2 weeks before planned display date; (c) order quantities based on: (i) historical sell-through rate by SKU by season; (ii) store&#x27;s garden center display capacity (shelf/ground space); (iii) local demographic preferences (urban stores sell more indoor plants; rural stores sell more vegetables and fruit trees)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/week during peak</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1119_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1119_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1119_Task8" name="Live Plant Receiving &amp; Quality Inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Live Plant Receiving &amp; Quality Inspection: (a) Stock Associate receives plant delivery from nursery supplier: (i) inspects each tray/pot for: healthy foliage (no yellowing, wilting, or pest damage), moist soil, intact root system (gently tug plant to verify root establishment), correct species/variety label; (ii) rejects substandard plants at receiving — driver returns rejected plants to nursery (no credit note needed as plants were not accepted); (iii) records receipt in ERP: item, quantity, supplier, date; (b) plants staged in garden center in designated display areas: (i) sun-loving plants in full sun area; (ii) shade-loving plants under canopy or shade cloth; (iii) indoor plants positioned near store entrance for visibility; (c) plant labels and price tags applied per W63 (shelf label &amp; price tag distribution)
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30–60 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1119_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1119_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1119_Task9" name="Daily Plant Maintenance &amp; Inventory Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Daily Plant Maintenance &amp; Inventory Monitoring: (a) Sales Associate performs daily garden center maintenance: (i) watering: early morning (6:00–7:00 AM) before store opens, adjusted for weather (extra watering during hot days, reduced during rainy periods); (ii) pruning: remove dead leaves/flowers, trim leggy growth; (iii) pest inspection: check for aphids, mealybugs, whiteflies; isolate and treat affected plants; (iv) rotation: move plants to ensure even sun exposure; (v) cleanup: remove fallen leaves, spilled soil, empty pots; (b) daily inventory scan: Associate scans plant barcode/QR during maintenance to update system on: (i) current on-hand quantity; (ii) plant condition (healthy, declining, distressed); (iii) days since receipt; (c) system alerts when plants approach end of shelf life: (i) 7 days before: &quot;Monitor&quot; alert; (ii) 3 days before: &quot;Markdown recommended&quot; alert; (iii) past shelf life: &quot;Remove &amp; compost&quot; alert
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30–45 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1119_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1119_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1119_Task10" name="Progressive Markdown &amp; Clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Progressive Markdown &amp; Clearance: (a) system auto-triggers markdown for aging plants: (i) 7+ days since receipt: 20% markdown — price tag updated, clearance label applied; (ii) 10+ days: 40% markdown; (iii) 14+ days: 60% markdown; (iv) past shelf life (species-dependent, typically 14–21 days): remove from sales floor; (b) markdown plants moved to designated &quot;Garden Clearance&quot; rack for visibility; (c) all markdowns tracked in system for category-level margin analysis; (d) end-of-season clearance event (W93): remaining seasonal plants marked down 50–70% in a coordinated promotion
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–20 min/day for markdowns</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1119_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1119_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1119_Task11" name="Unsold Plant Disposition &amp; Composting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Unsold Plant Disposition &amp; Composting: (a) plants past shelf life or unsellable condition (diseased, severely wilted) are removed from sales floor: (i) inventory write-off in system per W92 (inventory adjustment &amp; shrinkage authorization); (ii) healthy plant waste composted on-site if store has space, or collected by organic waste hauler per W502; (iii) plastic pots and trays cleaned and returned to nursery supplier for reuse (sustainability initiative per W193); (b) write-off value tracked by Category Manager for: (i) supplier quality assessment (high write-off rate = poor nursery quality); (ii) assortment decision (high write-off variety = discontinue); (iii) seasonal demand calibration (adjust next season&#x27;s order quantities); (c) monthly garden center shrinkage report generated per store and consolidated
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–20 min/disposition cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1119_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1119_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1119_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1119_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1119_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Department Supervisor (Garden &amp; Outdoor)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1119_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1119_Annotation13" targetRef="W1119_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1119_Flow15" sourceRef="W1119_Start6" targetRef="W1119_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1119_Flow16" sourceRef="W1119_Task7" targetRef="W1119_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1119_Flow17" sourceRef="W1119_Task8" targetRef="W1119_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1119_Flow18" sourceRef="W1119_Task9" targetRef="W1119_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1119_Flow19" sourceRef="W1119_Task10" targetRef="W1119_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1119_Flow20" sourceRef="W1119_Task11" targetRef="W1119_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
