    <bpmn:process id="W_W1135" name="W1135. Store-Level Daily Temperature-Sensitive Product Monitoring &amp; Quality Check" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily opening procedure (W5A), or temperature alert from monitoring device, or product quality concern reported
Frequency: Daily (200 stores × 365 days)
Volume: ~30–50 temperature-sensitive SKUs per store
Owner: Department Supervisor (relevant department)
Participants: Stock Associate, Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1135 — Store-Level Daily Temperature-Sensitive Product Monitoring &amp; Quality Check</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1135_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1135_Lane1" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1135_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1135_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1135_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1135_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1135_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1135_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1135_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1135_Start4" name="Daily opening procedure (W5A), or temperature alert from monitoring device, or product…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1135_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1135_Task5" name="Daily Temperature Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily Temperature Check: (a) during store opening (W5A), Stock Associate records ambient temperature in key store zones: indoor selling floor, outdoor lumber yard, paint section, garden center, receiving dock, backroom storage; (b) temperature logged in ERP via mobile app or store tablet; (c) automated temperature sensors (if installed) provide continuous monitoring with alert thresholds; (d) focus on high-risk zones: paint mixing station area (should be &lt; 35°C), outdoor garden center (shade structures checked), backroom chemical storage
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1135_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1135_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1135_Task6" name="Product Condition Spot Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product Condition Spot Check: (a) Stock Associate visually inspects temperature-sensitive products: paint cans — check for bulging lids (indicates gas buildup from heat), leaking, or label discoloration; adhesives/sealants — squeeze test for proper consistency (not hardened or runny); PVC pipes — check for warping or discoloration; batteries — check for leaking or corrosion on terminals; garden seeds — check display for heat damage (wilting, mold); (b) any concerns documented with photos in ERP
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1135_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1135_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1135_Task7" name="Corrective Action for Temperature Excursion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Corrective Action for Temperature Excursion: (a) if temperature exceeds acceptable range: move affected products to cooler area (indoor backroom with fans/ventilation); (b) for outdoor products: deploy shade structures (awning, shade cloth) over garden center and paint display area; (c) for paint: activate air conditioning or fans in paint section during extreme heat (March–May); (d) products showing quality degradation: quarantine and markdown per W549 (damaged/open-box processing) or disposition per W91 (damaged goods); (e) system logs temperature excursion event for vendor notification (if product quality claim needed) and shrinkage tracking (W845)
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1135_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1135_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1135_Task8" name="Seasonal Preparedness &amp; Facility Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Seasonal Preparedness &amp; Facility Improvement: (a) before summer peak (February): verify air conditioning units in paint section are operational; install shade structures in outdoor areas; review product placement — move heat-sensitive items away from direct sunlight and exterior walls; (b) before rainy season (May): check for water leaks that could affect product storage; verify drainage in outdoor areas; (c) facility improvement requests submitted per W47 (store facility maintenance) for permanent solutions: improved ventilation, air conditioning upgrades, shade structure installation
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min (seasonal)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1135_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1135_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1135_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1135_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1135_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (relevant department) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (relevant department)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1135_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1135_Annotation10" targetRef="W1135_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
