    <bpmn:process id="W_W1192" name="W1192. Post-Typhoon Store Damage Assessment, Insurance Claim &amp; Rapid Reopening Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA lowers typhoon signal below Storm Signal No. 1 for store&#x27;s area; or NDRRMC declares all-clear for the area
Frequency: ~3–5 events/year affecting subsets of the 200-store chain; any individual store may be affected 0–2 times/year
Volume: During a major typhoon: 20–80 stores may be simultaneously affected requiring assessment
Owner: VP Store Operations
Participants: Store Manager, VP Store Operations, Maintenance Engineer, Insurance Coordinator, Regional Manager, Facilities Team, CFO (insurance claims &gt; PHP 500K)
Source: workflow W1192 — Post-Typhoon Store Damage Assessment, Insurance Claim &amp; Rapid Reopening Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1192_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1192_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1192_Lane2" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1192_Lane3" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1192_Lane4" name="Maintenance Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1192_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1192_Start6" name="PAGASA lowers typhoon signal below Storm Signal No. 1 for store&#x27;s area; or NDRRMC…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task7" name="Post-storm safety clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Post-storm safety clearance: After PAGASA lowers signal: Store Manager (or designated staff if SM is unavailable) proceeds to store with safety kit (flashlight, hard hat, gloves, first aid); conducts exterior perimeter check for downed power lines, flooding, structural damage; does NOT enter building if structural damage is suspected; contacts VP Store Operations with initial &quot;Go / No-Go&quot; status
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task8" name="Damage assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Damage assessment: If Step 1 is &quot;Go&quot;: Store Manager enters store and conducts standardized damage assessment using mobile form: (a) roof integrity (leaks, missing sheets, structural deformation), (b) flooding level and extent (cm measurement at lowest point), (c) structural damage (walls, columns, beams, loading dock), (d) electrical system status (main panel, wiring, outlets, POS terminals), (e) inventory damage (water-damaged merchandise count by category), (f) equipment damage (forklifts, paint mixing machine, compressors), (g) exterior damage (signage, fence, lumber yard cover, parking area); captures photos and video of all damage; uploads to ERP disaster assessment module
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–4 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task9" name="Damage classification and escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Damage classification and escalation: VP Store Operations classifies each store: Green (minor damage, can open within 24 hours — e.g., minor leaks, no structural concern), Yellow (moderate damage, can open in 2–5 days with repairs — e.g., significant roof repair needed, partial flooding), Red (major damage, requires engineer assessment, closed &gt; 5 days — e.g., structural compromise, severe flooding &gt; 1 meter, electrical system damage); assigns Maintenance Engineer to Yellow and Red stores
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 hour (all affected stores)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task10" name="Insurance claim initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Insurance claim initiation: For Yellow and Red stores: Insurance Coordinator files preliminary insurance claim within 48 hours per insurance policy requirements: (a) notifies insurance company via hotline/email, (b) submits preliminary damage assessment report with photos from Step 2, (c) obtains claim reference number, (d) schedules insurance adjuster visit within 5 business days; for claims &gt; PHP 500K: CFO reviews and approves claim before submission
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task11" name="Emergency repair prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Emergency repair prioritization: Maintenance Engineer prioritizes emergency repairs for fastest possible reopening: (a) safety-critical first (electrical, structural shoring, roof patching), (b) operational-critical second (POS system, lighting, water drainage), (c) cosmetic last (signage, painting); for Green stores: Store Manager handles minor repairs with local contractor; for Yellow/Red: Maintenance Engineer dispatches facilities team or emergency contractor
Responsible (R): Maintenance Engineer
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Varies (4–48 hours)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task12" name="Inventory salvage and disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Inventory salvage and disposition: Store Manager separates damaged inventory: (a) water-damaged but sellable at discount → route to W91 (damaged goods disposition) for markdown per W93, (b) unsalvageable (waterlogged cement, swollen wood, rusted hardware) → quarantine for insurance documentation then disposal per W502/W82, (c) undamaged inventory → clean and reshelve; system updates inventory status for affected items
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Inventory Accountant
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–8 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task13" name="Controlled reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Controlled reopening: Once safety-critical and operational-critical repairs are complete: (a) Maintenance Engineer confirms store is safe for occupancy, (b) Store Manager verifies POS system operational, (c) VP Store Operations authorizes reopening, (d) store opens with potentially reduced operating hours or limited product sections; system sends reopening notification to customers via app/SMS per marketing protocol
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 hour/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1192_Task14" name="Insurance claim finalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Insurance claim finalization: After insurance adjuster visit and repair completion: Insurance Coordinator finalizes claim with: (a) final repair cost invoices, (b) inventory loss documentation with supporting GR/PO records, (c) business interruption calculation (days closed × daily revenue average), (d) adjuster report; tracks claim until settlement received; claims &gt; PHP 1M require CFO escalation to insurance broker
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–8 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1192_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1192_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1192_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1192_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: designating backup assessor (Assistant Store Manager) and regional &quot;flying squad&quot; of pre-designated assessment teams; operational: standardized mobile form in Step 2 and 48-hour preliminary filing in Step 4; operational: pre-negotiated emergency repair agreements and leveraging BuildRight&#x27;s own vendor relationships
Owner: VP Store Operations</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1192_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1192_Annotation16" targetRef="W1192_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow18" sourceRef="W1192_Start6" targetRef="W1192_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow19" sourceRef="W1192_Task7" targetRef="W1192_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow20" sourceRef="W1192_Task8" targetRef="W1192_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow21" sourceRef="W1192_Task9" targetRef="W1192_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow22" sourceRef="W1192_Task10" targetRef="W1192_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow23" sourceRef="W1192_Task11" targetRef="W1192_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow24" sourceRef="W1192_Task12" targetRef="W1192_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow25" sourceRef="W1192_Task13" targetRef="W1192_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1192_Flow26" sourceRef="W1192_Task14" targetRef="W1192_End15" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1192_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1192_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1192">
