    <bpmn:process id="W_W1297" name="W1297. Store-Level Perimeter Security &amp; Parking Lot Safety Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store operations cycle; or security incident in parking lot or store perimeter
Frequency: Daily monitoring; weekly patrol review; monthly security report
Volume: 200 stores with outdoor lumber yards and customer parking lots; ~2–5 formally-reportable security incidents per store per year (per W471)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Security Guard (contracted), Maintenance/Utility, Loss Prevention Officer
Source: workflow W1297 — Store-Level Perimeter Security &amp; Parking Lot Safety Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1297_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1297_Lane1" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1297_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1297_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1297_Start4" name="Daily store operations cycle; or security incident in parking lot or store perimeter">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task5" name="Opening security sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Opening security sweep: Security Guard conducts perimeter security sweep before store opening: (a) check perimeter fencing/wall for breach or damage, (b) verify all gates locked overnight and undisturbed, (c) inspect lumber yard for signs of overnight theft or vandalism, (d) check parking lot for abandoned vehicles or suspicious items, (e) verify CCTV cameras operational (lumber yard, parking lot, receiving dock, main entrance), (f) report findings to Store Manager before opening authorization
Responsible (R): Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task6" name="Parking lot safety monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Parking lot safety monitoring: During store hours: (a) Security Guard monitors parking lot for: suspicious loitering, vehicle break-in attempts, customer loading of oversized items (validate against purchase receipt), (b) Maintenance/Utility inspects parking lot hazards: potholes, standing water, loose debris, inadequate lighting at dusk, (c) for evening hours: ensure parking lot lighting fully operational, (d) manage vehicle flow during peak hours (weekends, sale events per W262) to prevent congestion and accidents
Responsible (R): Security Guard / Maintenance
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task7" name="Lumber yard access control">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Lumber yard access control: Security Guard monitors lumber yard area: (a) all customers entering lumber yard pass through designated entry point, (b) customers exiting lumber yard with merchandise must have purchase receipt or be directed to checkout, (c) for large lumber purchases: Security Guard verifies receipt matches loaded merchandise before customer exits yard, (d) after hours: lumber yard gate secured and locked; CCTV monitoring continues
Responsible (R): Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task8" name="CCTV monitoring &amp; incident response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: CCTV monitoring &amp; incident response: Security Guard monitors CCTV feeds: (a) lumber yard camera (high-theft area), (b) parking lot cameras (customer safety, vehicle security), (c) receiving dock (vendor and delivery activity), (d) main entrance (customer count, suspicious behavior per W405), (e) for incidents: Security Guard responds per protocol: (i) theft in progress: confront and detain if safe, call police if aggressive, (ii) vehicle break-in: call police, secure scene, assist customer, (iii) customer injury: provide first aid, document incident per W440, call emergency services if needed
Responsible (R): Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task9" name="Closing security procedure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Closing security procedure: At store closing: (a) Security Guard conducts final perimeter sweep of all areas, (b) verify all customers have exited store and lumber yard, (c) secure all entry points: front doors, lumber yard gate, receiving dock, emergency exits ( alarmed), (d) activate after-hours alarm system, (e) Security Guard remains on-site overnight (24-hour security coverage per contract) or activates remote alarm monitoring
Responsible (R): Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task10" name="Weekly security report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Weekly security report: Store Manager compiles weekly security summary: (a) incidents reported (theft, break-in, vandalism, customer complaints), (b) CCTV footage review findings, (c) parking lot safety issues identified and resolved, (d) security guard performance (attendance, incident response), (e) submit to Regional Loss Prevention Officer for inclusion in LP dashboard per W405
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional LP Officer
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1297_Task11" name="Monthly security review &amp; vendor coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly security review &amp; vendor coordination: Monthly, Store Manager meets with contracted security agency: (a) review incident log and response times, (b) discuss guard rotation and performance issues, (c) coordinate additional security for peak periods (sale events, holiday season, post-typhoon high-value inventory), (d) review and update security protocols based on incident trends, (e) Regional LP Officer participates quarterly for strategic security assessment per W839
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Agency
Accountable (A): Regional LP Officer
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1297_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1297_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1297_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1297_Annotation13">
