    <bpmn:process id="W_W1302" name="W1302. Typhoon Season Store Protection, Rapid Reopening &amp; Post-Disaster Assessment Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA Public Storm Warning Signal (PSWS) #1 or higher for any store location; or post-typhoon store damage assessment
Frequency: ~20 typhoons enter the Philippine Area of Responsibility (PAR) per year; ~8–10 directly affect BuildRight store locations; pre-typhoon preparations executed ~10–15 times/year; post-typhoon assessments ~5–8 times/year
Volume: Varies: Signal #1 may affect 20–40 stores; Signal #2–3 may affect 60–100 stores; Signal #4–5 may affect 100+ stores simultaneously
Owner: Regional Manager / Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Assistant Store Manager, Stock Associates, Security Guard, Regional Manager, COO, Facilities Coordinator, Insurance Coordinator
Source: workflow W1302 — Typhoon Season Store Protection, Rapid Reopening &amp; Post-Disaster Assessment Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1302_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1302_Lane1" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1302_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1302_Lane3" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1302_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1302_Start5" name="PAGASA Public Storm Warning Signal (PSWS) #1 or higher for any store location; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1302_Task6" name="PAGASA monitoring &amp; alert activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PAGASA monitoring &amp; alert activation: (a) Regional Manager monitors PAGASA weather bulletins during typhoon season (June–November); (b) when PAGASA raises PSWS #1 for any province containing BuildRight stores: Regional Manager activates Typhoon Preparation Protocol for affected stores; (c) system sends automated alerts to all affected Store Managers with: storm track forecast, expected wind speeds, expected rainfall, estimated time of landfall, preparation checklist
Responsible (R): Regional Manager / System
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Alert: immediate; Preparation: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1302_Task7" name="Pre-typhoon store protection (Signal #1–2)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-typhoon store protection (Signal #1–2): Affected Store Managers execute preparation checklist: (a) Outdoor inventory protection: (i) cover lumber stacks with heavy-duty tarps and secure with tie-downs, (ii) move small outdoor items (garden pots, potted plants) inside backroom, (iii) secure lightweight building materials (GI sheets, insulation) that could become airborne, (iv) lower outdoor display racks or secure with weights; (b) Building protection: (i) check roof drainage channels — clear debris to prevent water accumulation, (ii) install flood barriers at doors if store is in flood-prone area, (iii) check emergency generator fuel level and test startup, (iv) secure rooftop HVAC units and satellite dishes; (c) Inventory preparation: (i) reduce outdoor lumber yard inventory if advance notice ≥ 48 hours — expedite sales or move high-value items under cover, (ii) elevate bottom-shelf inventory in flood-prone areas by 30–60 cm, (iii) secure paint and chemical inventory to prevent spillage (DENR hazardous material protocol per W492); (d) Staff communication: (i) confirm staff contact information is current, (ii) announce store closure decision (Signal #2: optional closure at Store Manager discretion; Signal #3: mandatory closure per COO directive), (iii) assign skeleton crew for overnight security (Security Guard + 1 staff)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Stock Associates
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1302_Task8" name="Pre-typhoon escalation (Signal #3–5)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pre-typhoon escalation (Signal #3–5): For severe typhoons: (a) COO issues mandatory closure directive for all stores in affected areas; (b) Regional Manager coordinates with all affected Store Managers: (i) confirm all staff safely evacuated or at home, (ii) confirm store secured and alarm system active, (iii) confirm emergency generator operational (for security systems, CCTV, alarm), (c) HQ activates emergency operations center: (i) monitor store status via IoT sensors (water level, power status, temperature), (ii) coordinate with insurance broker for advance notice of potential claims, (iii) pre-position emergency supplies at regional offices (generator fuel, plywood for broken windows, water pumps)
Responsible (R): COO / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Continuous during storm</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1302_Task9" name="Post-typhoon rapid damage assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-typhoon rapid damage assessment: Within 6 hours of typhoon passage and PAGASA downgrading signal: (a) Store Manager (or designated staff if Store Manager cannot reach store) conducts rapid assessment: (i) structural: roof intact? walls intact? doors/windows intact? any structural compromise? (ii) flooding: water level inside store (measure in cm), is water receding or rising? (iii) inventory: outdoor yard damage assessment (lumber, building materials), indoor inventory water damage, (iv) utilities: power status (grid power or generator), water supply, telecom/internet connectivity, (v) safety: electrical hazards (downed wires, wet electrical panels), chemical spills (paint, solvents), structural hazards (collapsed shelving, broken glass); (b) Store Manager submits rapid assessment report via mobile app (offline-capable — report syncs when connectivity restored): Go (no significant damage, can open within 24 hours), Limited (some damage, partial operations possible within 48 hours), Major (significant damage, cannot open until repairs completed — target 3–7 days), Catastrophic (structural failure, safety hazard — do not enter until engineer inspection)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1302_Task10" name="Rapid reopening execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Rapid reopening execution: (a) for stores rated &quot;Go&quot;: Store Manager executes reopening protocol: (i) verify POS system operational (test transaction processing, check connectivity), (ii) verify all safety hazards remediated, (iii) remove protection measures (tarps, flood barriers), (iv) restock any displaced inventory, (v) notify staff of reopening schedule; (b) for stores rated &quot;Limited&quot;: Regional Manager dispatches facilities team: (i) temporary repairs (plywood over broken windows, tarp over roof leak), (ii) partial store opening (undamaged sections only), (iii) deploy backup POS terminal if primary damaged; (c) for stores rated &quot;Major&quot; or &quot;Catastrophic&quot;: COO activates disaster recovery plan: (i) dispatch construction team for emergency repairs, (ii) file insurance claim per W26, (iii) redirect customer traffic to nearest open store, (iv) communicate store status via social media and website (W142)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager / COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Go: 4–8 hours; Limited: 24–48 hours; Major: 3–7 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1302_Task11" name="Post-disaster inventory loss accounting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-disaster inventory loss accounting: (a) for damaged inventory: Store Manager conducts damage count by SKU: (i) water-damaged items (lumber, cardboard packaging, appliances) — typically write-off per W91, (ii) chemically contaminated items (paint/thinner containers compromised by flooding) — hazardous waste disposal per W492, (iii) missing/stolen items (looting risk during evacuation) — file police report per W471 and insurance claim per W26; (b) Finance Controller reviews damage reports: (i) total inventory loss by store, (ii) insurance claim amount per W26, (iii) net uninsured loss, (iv) post inventory write-off journal entries; (c) Category Manager adjusts replenishment plans for damaged categories to restock reopened stores quickly
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1302_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1302_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1302_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1302_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: Regional Manager / Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Regional Manager / Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1302_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1302_Annotation13" targetRef="W1302_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow15" sourceRef="W1302_Start5" targetRef="W1302_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow16" sourceRef="W1302_Task6" targetRef="W1302_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow17" sourceRef="W1302_Task7" targetRef="W1302_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow18" sourceRef="W1302_Task8" targetRef="W1302_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow19" sourceRef="W1302_Task9" targetRef="W1302_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow20" sourceRef="W1302_Task10" targetRef="W1302_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1302_Flow21" sourceRef="W1302_Task11" targetRef="W1302_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1302_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1302_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1302">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1302_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1302_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1302_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1302_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1302_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1302_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
