    <bpmn:process id="W_W1317" name="W1317. Store-Level Generator Backup Power Operations, Fuel Management &amp; Load Shedding Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Commercial power outage (brownout/blackout) at store location; or scheduled rotational brownout advisory from local electric cooperative
Frequency: ~1–2 unplanned outage/brownout events per store per month in affected areas (concentrated in the Mindanao dry season; ~800–1,500 chain-wide/year per W470, mitigated by generator backup); ~2–4 scheduled rotational brownouts per month in some areas during dry season
Volume: ~150 stores equipped with 1 backup diesel generator (50–100 kVA; per W741)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Maintenance/Utility Staff, Security Guard, Facilities Coordinator
Source: workflow W1317 — Store-Level Generator Backup Power Operations, Fuel Management &amp; Load Shedding Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1317_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1317_Lane1" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1317_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1317_Lane3" name="Facilities Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1317_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1317_Start5" name="Commercial power outage (brownout/blackout) at store location; or scheduled rotational…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1317_Task6" name="Generator startup &amp; load transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Generator startup &amp; load transfer: (a) when commercial power fails: (i) automatic transfer switch (ATS) detects power loss and signals generator to start, (ii) generator auto-starts and reaches stable output within 15–30 seconds, (iii) ATS transfers load to generator; (b) if ATS fails or generator does not auto-start: Maintenance/Utility Staff performs manual start per posted procedure; (c) Maintenance/Utility Staff verifies: (i) generator running smoothly (no unusual sounds or vibration), (ii) voltage output within acceptable range (220V ± 10%), (iii) critical loads powered: POS terminals (all 3), lighting (sales floor minimum), security systems (CCTV, alarm), customer service counter; (d) non-critical loads disconnected: air conditioning (reduce to minimum units), outdoor signage, non-essential lighting
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1317_Task7" name="Load shedding priority management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Load shedding priority management: (a) generator capacity (50–100 kVA) cannot power all store loads simultaneously; Maintenance/Utility Staff manages load shedding priority: Priority 1 (always powered): POS terminals, store server/network, security systems (CCTV, alarm), emergency lighting, fire suppression; Priority 2 (powered if capacity allows): sales floor lighting, paint mixing station, customer service counter, PA system; Priority 3 (powered only with excess capacity): air conditioning (minimum units), backroom lighting, outdoor signage; (b) Maintenance/Utility Staff monitors generator load gauge — if approaching 80% capacity: shed Priority 3 loads; if approaching 90%: shed Priority 2 loads except POS; (c) during extended outages (&gt;4 hours): cycle Priority 3 loads — run AC for 30 min, then switch to other Priority 3 loads
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Ongoing during outage</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1317_Task8" name="Fuel monitoring &amp; replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fuel monitoring &amp; replenishment: (a) Maintenance/Utility Staff monitors generator fuel gauge continuously during outage: (i) full tank (typically 100–200 liters diesel) provides 8–12 hours at typical load, (ii) at 50% fuel level: contact nearest fuel supplier for emergency delivery, (iii) at 25% fuel level: escalate to Regional Manager for fuel logistics coordination; (b) fuel replenishment: (i) Maintenance/Utility Staff or Security Guard travels to nearest gas station with approved fuel containers (20-liter jerry cans, stored at store), (ii) refuel generator during operation (most generators support hot refueling with safety precautions), (iii) record fuel purchase in ERP (receipt upload, cost allocation to store utilities budget); (c) monthly: Facilities Coordinator reviews generator fuel consumption per store — identify stores with excessive fuel costs (frequent outages or generator inefficiency)
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per refueling: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1317_Task9" name="Commercial power restoration &amp; generator shutdown">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Commercial power restoration &amp; generator shutdown: (a) when commercial power is restored: (i) ATS detects stable commercial power for ≥ 30 seconds (anti-islanding delay), (ii) ATS transfers load back to commercial power, (iii) generator runs unloaded for 3–5 minutes (cool-down period) then auto-shuts down; (b) Maintenance/Utility Staff performs post-outage checks: (i) verify all POS terminals reconnected to network and syncing, (ii) verify security systems on commercial power and recording, (iii) check generator for any issues during outage (leaks, overheating), (iv) record outage duration and generator run-hours in maintenance log
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1317_Task10" name="Scheduled rotational brownout preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Scheduled rotational brownout preparation: (a) when local electric cooperative announces scheduled rotational brownout: Store Manager prepares: (i) verify generator fuel level ≥ 75%, (ii) top up fuel if needed before scheduled outage, (iii) brief staff on load shedding protocol, (iv) pre-charge UPS backup for POS server (ensures no data loss during ATS transfer delay), (v) notify customers at entrance if outage will affect store operations (reduced AC, limited services)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min before scheduled outage</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1317_Task11" name="Quarterly generator maintenance &amp; testing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly generator maintenance &amp; testing: (a) Facilities Coordinator schedules quarterly generator maintenance per manufacturer schedule: (i) oil and filter change (every 200 run-hours or quarterly), (ii) coolant level check, (iii) battery load test (battery failure is #1 cause of generator no-start), (iv) fuel system inspection (water contamination in diesel is common in humid Philippine climate), (v) ATS functional test (simulate power failure to verify auto-start); (b) maintenance performed by contracted generator service provider per W47 (facility maintenance work orders); (c) stores with &gt;200 generator run-hours/year prioritized for maintenance; (d) generator replacement planning: units with &gt;5,000 run-hours or &gt;10 years age flagged for capital replacement per W21
Responsible (R): Facilities Coordinator / Service Provider
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/quarter per generator</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1317_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1317_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1317_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1317_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1317_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1317_Annotation13" targetRef="W1317_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
