    <bpmn:process id="W_W1505" name="W1505. Store-Level Typhoon &amp; Natural Disaster Preparation, Response &amp; Business Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA raises Tropical Cyclone Wind Signal (TCWS) over any store location; or Regional Operations Manager issues disaster preparedness advisory
Frequency: ~20 typhoons/year enter PAR; ~8–10 directly impact store locations; ~3–4 require full preparation protocols
Volume: Per typhoon event: 20–80 stores may be in the affected path; all 200 stores require annual typhoon readiness verification
Owner: Regional Operations Manager; Store Manager (execution)
Participants: Store Manager, Assistant Store Manager, Department Supervisors, Stock Associates, Security Guard, VP Store Operations, Logistics Manager, DC Manager, Facilities Coordinator, HR Manager
Source: workflow W1505 — Store-Level Typhoon &amp; Natural Disaster Preparation, Response &amp; Business Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1505_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1505_Lane1" name="Regional Ops Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1505_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1505_Lane3" name="Supply Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1505_Lane4" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1505_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1505_Start6" name="PAGASA raises Tropical Cyclone Wind Signal (TCWS) over any store location; or Regional…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1505_Task7" name="PAGASA monitoring &amp; alert escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PAGASA monitoring &amp; alert escalation: Regional Operations Manager monitors PAGASA tropical cyclone advisories daily during typhoon season (June–November); when TCWS #1 is raised over any store location: (a) System auto-generates &quot;Typhoon Alert Level 1&quot; notification to all Store Managers in the affected region; (b) Regional Ops Manager reviews projected track and timing; (c) if TCWS #2 or higher is projected within 48 hours: escalate to Alert Level 2 and initiate preparation protocol
Responsible (R): Regional Ops Mgr / System
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task8" name="Alert Level 2 — 48-hour preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Alert Level 2 — 48-hour preparation: For all stores in projected path: (a) Store Manager conducts inventory of emergency supplies: flashlights, batteries, first aid kits per W501, generator fuel, drinking water (3 days supply for 29 staff), non-perishable food; (b) verify backup generator operational per W470; (c) test POS offline capability — ensure each terminal has ≥ 8 hours offline capacity per NFR-011; (d) Facilities Coordinator schedules pre-typhoon building inspection: roof anchors, signage mounting, outdoor lumber yard securing, drainage clearance; (e) confirm satellite phone or two-way radio availability (cellular network disruption expected)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Facilities Coordinator
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task9" name="Alert Level 3 — 24-hour intensive preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Alert Level 3 — 24-hour intensive preparation: When TCWS #3+ is raised: (a) outdoor lumber yard: Stock Associates secure all loose materials, stack lumber flat, cover with tarpaulins weighted by sandbags; (b) outdoor tile/display area: move display units indoors or lay flat and secure; (c) storefront: remove or secure all outdoor signage, banner stands, and promotional flags; (d) backroom: elevate bottom-shelf inventory to ≥ 1 meter (flood risk); move high-value items (power tools, appliances) to highest shelves; (e) IT: verify last data sync completed; confirm offline POS cache is current; (f) cash: mid-day cash skimming per W278 — reduce cash on hand to minimum float; transfer excess to safe or CIT pickup; (g) employee safety: Store Manager releases non-essential staff; retains skeleton crew of 5–8 for final securing; confirms all staff have safe transportation home; (h) Logistics: cancel or redirect inbound deliveries to stores in safe zones
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Stock Associates / Cashier
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 8–12 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task10" name="During-typhoon protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: During-typhoon protocol: Store is closed to public; skeleton crew remains only if safe to do so: (a) continuous PAGASA monitoring via battery-powered radio; (b) hourly building condition check: roof leaks, flooding in yard, structural integrity; (c) if building integrity threatened: full evacuation per W330; (d) document all damage with timestamped photos for insurance claims per W610; (e) communicate status to Regional Ops Manager every 4 hours (or when safe) via satellite phone/SMS
Responsible (R): Store Manager (skeleton crew)
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: Duration of typhoon</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task11" name="Post-typhoon damage assessment (T+0 to T+24)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-typhoon damage assessment (T+0 to T+24): Once PAGASA downgrades TCWS and local government declares area safe: (a) Store Manager and Department Supervisors conduct full damage assessment: (i) structural damage (roof, walls, doors, windows), (ii) inventory damage (water exposure, fallen items, contamination), (iii) equipment damage (POS terminals, refrigeration for paint, forklift), (iv) outdoor yard damage (lumber, building materials, fencing); (b) photograph all damage for insurance documentation; (c) categorize damage severity: (i) Level A — minor (cosmetic, reopenable within 24 hours), (ii) Level B — moderate (partial inventory loss, requires 2–5 days for cleanup and restocking), (iii) Level C — severe (structural damage, requires professional assessment, weeks to reopen); (d) submit Damage Assessment Report to Regional Ops Manager via system or email
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Dept Supervisor
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task12" name="Insurance claim initiation (T+24 to T+72)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Insurance claim initiation (T+24 to T+72): For Level B and C damage: (a) Regional Ops Manager submits insurance notification to Finance per W610; (b) Finance prepares claim documentation: damage photos, inventory loss report from ERP, structural engineer assessment (Level C), repair estimates; (c) coordinate with loss insurance adjuster for site visit within 7 days; (d) for business interruption claims: document days closed and estimated revenue loss from prior year same-period sales data
Responsible (R): Regional Ops Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 8–16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task13" name="Business recovery — store reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Business recovery — store reopening: (a) Level A stores: cleanup (6–12 hours), restock from backroom, verify POS connectivity, reopen next business day; (b) Level B stores: (i) engage professional cleanup crew, (ii) process inventory write-offs for damaged goods per W93 markdown or full write-off, (iii) submit emergency restock request to DC — prioritize essential items (construction materials for community rebuilding, roofing, nails, tarps, water tanks), (iv) temporary reduced hours for first week; (c) Level C stores: (i) engage contractor per W96 (store renovation), (ii) consider temporary popup or redirect customers to nearest open store, (iii) communicate alternative store locations to affected customers via SMS/email; (d) all reopened stores: verify POS system operational, run inventory reconciliation, report open status to Regional Ops Manager dashboard
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Ops Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day (Level A) to 4–8 weeks (Level C)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task14" name="Post-disaster community demand surge management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-disaster community demand surge management: After major typhoons, demand for construction and rebuilding materials surges 300–500% in affected areas: (a) Supply Planning team adjusts demand forecasts per SCP-001 for affected stores; (b) DC prioritizes outbound shipments of roofing, plywood, cement, nails, tarps, water tanks to affected region; (c) Merchandising activates emergency pricing protocol — consider price freeze compliance per POS-024 (DTI may issue price freeze on prime commodities in disaster-declared areas); (d) coordinate with vendor partners for emergency import or expedited delivery of reconstruction materials; (e) Stores Manager monitors stock levels daily and communicates shortages to Merchandising
Responsible (R): Supply Planning / Merchandising / VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Continuous (2–8 weeks post-disaster)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1505_Task15" name="Post-event review &amp; preparedness improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-event review &amp; preparedness improvement: Within 30 days of a major typhoon event: (a) VP Store Operations convenes post-event review with Regional Ops Managers, DC Managers, Supply Planning, Facilities, and HR; (b) review: preparation effectiveness, employee safety outcomes, inventory damage vs. prevention, supply chain response time, community demand fulfillment, insurance claim processing time; (c) update Typhoon Preparedness Protocol based on lessons learned; (d) identify stores requiring structural reinforcement or flood mitigation investment; (e) update emergency supply inventory levels; (f) schedule annual pre-typhoon season readiness audit (May) across all 200 stores
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Regional Ops Mgr
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours (review meeting)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1505_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1505_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1505_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1505_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: standardized preparation checklists (Steps 2–3) that Store Managers execute autonomously and a clear alert escalation protocol; operational: seasonal/temporary staffing protocol per W172 and cross-training per W567; operational: per POS-024
Owner: Regional Operations Manager; Store Manager (execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1505_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1505_Annotation17" targetRef="W1505_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1505_Flow19" sourceRef="W1505_Start6" targetRef="W1505_Task7" />
