    <bpmn:process id="W_W5536" name="W5536. Missing-Child / Code Adam In-Store Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A parent, guardian, or companion reports a child (under 12) missing inside the store premises; or an unaccompanied, distressed, or apparently lost child is found by staff; or a suspected attempted-abduction is observed
Frequency: Rare; ~5–15 separations resolved at the service desk weekly chain-wide (minutes, self-resolved); ~2–6 formal Code-Adam activations per year chain-wide
Volume: 1 store × full team (29 staff/store) × the ~99,000 customers on premises chain-wide per operating day (W330 population canon) — family shoppers with children are a core BuildRight demographic
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, all floor staff (zone search), Front-End/Service Desk (guardian liaison), Security Guard (door control, CCTV), LP Officer, Regional Manager (escalation), PNP (911) &amp; PNP-Women and Children Protection Desk, barangay, VP Legal (evidence/liability), HR (staff trauma support per W717 debrief practice)
Source: workflow W5536 — Missing-Child / Code Adam In-Store Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5536_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5536_Lane1" name="Service Desk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5536_Lane2" name="Zone staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5536_Lane3" name="Yard staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5536_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5536_Lane5" name="All Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5536_Lane6" name="Duty Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5536_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5536_Start8" name="A parent, guardian, or companion reports a child (under 12) missing inside the store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task9" name="Report receipt &amp; Code-Adam activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Report receipt &amp; Code-Adam activation: Service Desk takes the guardian&#x27;s report (child&#x27;s name, age, clothing, hair/eye color, where/when last seen); Manager announces the activation — coded PA script stating description only (no &quot;missing&quot;/&quot;abducted&quot; wording), all staff stop routine tasks; door alert: front-end holds transactions near exits and positions staff at every customer exit (front, garden, yard, fire exits with alarms) — no child exits unaccompanied until stand-down
Responsible (R): Service Desk / Front-End
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: &lt; 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task10" name="Zone search — interior">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Zone search — interior: assigned staff systematically search their own zones (staff search areas they know): aisle ends, display fixtures, furniture/tent setups, restrooms (call-out check), fitting areas, stockroom, receiving, staff areas, battery/tool kiosks — 5-minute sweep, report found/clear to Manager by radio
Responsible (R): Zone staff / Duty Supervisors
Accountable (A): Duty Supervisors
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task11" name="Zone search — exterior">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Zone search — exterior: yard/lumber zones, garden center, parking aisles, cart corrals, landscaping; Security sweeps the perimeter and reviews live CCTV (entrances, exits, aisle cameras) from last-seen-time forward
Responsible (R): Yard staff / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Security Guard
Duration: 5–10 min (parallel)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task12" name="Found — reunification with verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Found — reunification with verification: child brought to Service Desk; comfort protocol (second adult present throughout — safeguarding rule); release only to the reporting guardian after identity/description match (and check the custodial-dispute flag: if a custody dispute is known or claimed, do not release — police decide); log time, persons present, and verification basis
Responsible (R): Service Desk / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task13" name="Not found at 10 minutes — police escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Not found at 10 minutes — police escalation: Manager calls 911/PNP; requests PNP-WCPD protocol handling; provides description, CCTV snapshot, last-seen point; store search continues under police direction; guardian stays with a dedicated staff liaison; VP Legal informed; CCTV footage preservation requested per the W471 evidence chain
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: At the 10-minute mark</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task14" name="Special branches">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Special branches: (a) unaccompanied child found → safeguarding rule, two-adult supervision, no release without verified guardian or police, PNP-WCPD if no guardian within 30 min; (b) suspected/attempted abduction or custody grab → do not confront, observe and report, 911 immediately, treat as W471 Category-A crime scene, preserve CCTV, W717/W140 support for involved staff
Responsible (R): All Staff / LP / VP Legal
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5536_Task15" name="Stand-down &amp; documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Stand-down &amp; documentation: deactivation PA; log the event (times, zones searched, outcome, reunification verification) into the W471 incident record even when resolved internally; guardian thank-you and service-recovery per store practice; debrief within 48 hours — response-time gaps and unswept-zone findings feed the W158 drill rotation (Code-Adam tabletop semi-annually per store)
Responsible (R): Duty Supervisors / Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hrs + debrief</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5536_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5536_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5536_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5536_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: two-adult rule for any found/unaccompanied child; release only after verified guardian match or police direction | - operational: every activation — including internally-resolved ones — is documented to the W471 incident record
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5536_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5536_Annotation17" targetRef="W5536_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow19" sourceRef="W5536_Start8" targetRef="W5536_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow20" sourceRef="W5536_Task9" targetRef="W5536_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow21" sourceRef="W5536_Task10" targetRef="W5536_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow22" sourceRef="W5536_Task11" targetRef="W5536_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow23" sourceRef="W5536_Task12" targetRef="W5536_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow24" sourceRef="W5536_Task13" targetRef="W5536_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow25" sourceRef="W5536_Task14" targetRef="W5536_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5536_Flow26" sourceRef="W5536_Task15" targetRef="W5536_End16" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W5536_diag">
