    <bpmn:process id="W_W5539" name="W5539. Elevator &amp; Escalator Entrapment Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Passenger(s) trapped in a stopped elevator car (between floors or doors blocked), or an escalator entrapment event (clothing/shoe caught at comb plate, fall on the unit, handrail incident)
Frequency: Rare; ~5–15 entrapment stoppages chain-wide per year across the multi-level stores (elevator incidents run ~1–3/unit/yr industry-wide); escalator incidents mostly minor
Volume: 1 unit × passengers on board (2–15 people) + responding store team; every event involves the licensed elevator-maintenance contractor under the W47 service contract
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Facilities/Maintenance Technician, elevator-maintenance contractor 24/7 emergency line (licensed technician), Security Guard, trained first-aider (W501), EMS (medical cases), DOLE-accredited elevator inspector (post-event, reportable cases), VP Legal (liability/evidence)
Source: workflow W5539 — Elevator &amp; Escalator Entrapment Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5539_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane1" name="First responder">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane2" name="Facilities Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane3" name="First Aider">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane4" name="Security">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane5" name="Contractor Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane6" name="Contractor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5539_Lane7" name="Facilities Standards Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5539_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5539_Start9" name="Passenger(s) trapped in a stopped elevator car (between floors or doors blocked), or an…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task10" name="Establish contact &amp; reassurance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Establish contact &amp; reassurance: respond to car alarm/interphone or staff report; two-way contact with passengers — keep them calm, instruct all to stand clear of the doors, never attempt to exit; establish count and condition (children, elderly, medical needs, panic)
Responsible (R): First responder / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: &lt; 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task11" name="Contractor emergency callout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Contractor emergency callout: call the maintenance contractor&#x27;s 24/7 line (W47 service contract); log the call time; urban SLA ≤ 60 min on-site, provincial ≤ 120 min; facilities technician assigned to wait at the unit; incident clock started
Responsible (R): Facilities Technician
Accountable (A): Facilities Coordinator
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task12" name="Medical-vulnerability triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Medical-vulnerability triage: continuous interphone check-ins every 10 min; if any passenger reports medical distress (or the projected wait exceeds ~45–60 min with vulnerable passengers): EMS per W501 immediately; if EMS assessment says extrication cannot wait for the contractor → BFP extrication (they have the authority/equipment); Store Manager makes the call and documents it
Responsible (R): First Aider / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task13" name="Area control &amp; power discipline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Area control &amp; power discipline: barricade the landings, keep crowds back, no one touches the machine room, mains/phase-failure switches operated only by the technician; if the car is between floors, door-force attempts are prohibited (the car may shift)
Responsible (R): Security / Facilities Technician
Accountable (A): Facilities Coordinator
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task14" name="Licensed release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Licensed release: contractor technician opens the car and landing doors, verifies car level, and walks passengers out; first-aider offers assessment per W501 (offer even if declined — document); Facilities logs release time
Responsible (R): Contractor Technician / First Aider
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–30 min after arrival</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task15" name="Escalator variant">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Escalator variant: landing stop buttons pressed (each landing end), power isolated by technician only; free the caught item (comb-plate reversal/disassembly is the technician&#x27;s); injured customers → W501 first aid + W285/W147.3 customer-incident chain; unit stays out of service until the technician re-sets and tests comb plates/handrail
Responsible (R): Facilities Technician / First Aider
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–90 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task16" name="Return-to-service &amp; documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Return-to-service &amp; documentation: technician&#x27;s incident report (cause: power phase loss, door sensor, brake, overload) filed to the unit&#x27;s asset history in W47; unit returns to service only after technician testing; injury/extended-exposure events documented per W140 (employee) and W147.3/W285 (customer) chains; DOLE-accredited inspector notified where the event involves a reportable safety-device failure
Responsible (R): Contractor / Facilities Coordinator
Accountable (A): Facilities Coordinator
Duration: 1–2 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5539_Task17" name="Recurrence review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Recurrence review: a unit with 2+ entrapments in 12 months triggers an engineering review — modernization vs continued repair via the W21 capex path (elevator modernization &gt; PHP 50K → W21); review results feed the W47 PM program and the contractor SLA review
Responsible (R): Facilities Standards Manager
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5539_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5539_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5539_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5539_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: passengers are released only by the licensed contractor technician; the machine room and mains switches are technician-only | - operational: medical-vulnerability check-ins run on a documented ≤ 10-minute clock with an EMS/BFP escalation decision point
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5539_Assoc20" sourceRef="W5539_Annotation19" targetRef="W5539_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
