    <bpmn:process id="W_W5561" name="W5561. Sustained Water-Service Interruption Response &amp; Store Continuity Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Water-utility notice or sudden loss of piped water service at a store or DC expected to exceed one trading day — service interruption, El Niño rationing, a district main break, or a pressure-loss/boil-water advisory from the utility or LGU
Frequency: Clustered utility event: dry-season rationing years (El Niño) produce multi-day interruptions across Metro Manila and water-district-served provincial sites; non-drought years see isolated main-break events — plan on the utility-notice lifecycle a handful of times per year chain-wide, with rationing episodes recurring on El Niño cycles
Volume: 1 event × affected sites (a single main break = 1–3 sites; a rationing episode = every site on the affected district, potentially dozens) × the water-dependent surface (restrooms, the ~200 garden centers&#x27; live goods per VS-145, fabrication cooling, cleaning, food-and-beverage concessions per W177) × duration tiers (1–10 days)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Regional Manager (multi-site events), Facilities/Maintenance (W47), HSE Manager (sanitation decisions, VS-24), Garden Center lead (VS-145 live-goods protection), Store Communications (VS-63 cascade), Procurement (emergency trucked-water sourcing, the W1187 class), LGU health/sanitation office and the utility (VS-166 permit interface), Cash Office (restricted-services tender handling if needed)
Source: workflow W5561 — Sustained Water-Service Interruption Response &amp; Store Continuity Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5561_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5561_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5561_Lane2" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5561_Lane3" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5561_Lane4" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5561_Lane5" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5561_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5561_Start7" name="Water-utility notice or sudden loss of piped water service at a store or DC expected to…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task8" name="Classify the interruption">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Classify the interruption: utility notice and restoration estimate; potable vs non-potable availability; affected-site census across the district; duration tier (≤ 1 day / 1–3 days / rationing mode &gt; 3 days) drives every later decision
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Facilities
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task9" name="Sanitation &amp; health decisions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sanitation &amp; health decisions: restroom status — full closure with portable-toilet rental via emergency PO, vs reduced service with enhanced hand-hygiene stations — decided with HSE sign-off under the sanitation-permit obligations (VS-166) and DOH/LGU sanitation standards; document either way
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HSE
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task10" name="Water-dependent service matrix">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Water-dependent service matrix: garden-center live-goods watering priority per VS-145 (perishable-stock protection, the W1387 inventory-elevation analog); fabrication/cooling services status; cleaning suspended to hygiene minimums; food-and-beverage concessions (W177) suspended where handwashing and dishwashing standards cannot be met
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors / Garden Center Lead
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task11" name="Emergency water operations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Emergency water operations: trucked-water sourcing and delivery prioritization across affected sites (W1187-class emergency PO with pre-qualified water vendors); on-site storage refill; conservation directives to all departments
Responsible (R): Procurement / Facilities
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Daily, event-long</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task12" name="Customer &amp; employee communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer &amp; employee communication: service-status signage (restrooms closed, services limited) without overpromising restoration times; store-communications cascade per VS-63; drinking-water provision for staff as a welfare duty (VS-19.1-class)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task13" name="Trading-continuity decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Trading-continuity decision: trade-with-restrictions is the default; partial-closure or closure decisions ride the Regional Manager closure authority (the E-02 custody — W2510 decides, W850 executes) when sanitation standards cannot be maintained; the decision is documented either way
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations (multi-site)
Duration: On threshold</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task14" name="Recovery &amp; flush protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Recovery &amp; flush protocol: on restoration — system flush per utility/LGU guidance; boil-water advisory handling for any food-related water use; water-quality confirmation before restroom and food-service reopening; sanitation-permit records updated (VS-166)
Responsible (R): Facilities / HSE
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5561_Task15" name="Duration escalation &amp; after-action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Duration escalation &amp; after-action: multi-day events engage the BCP reporting layer (the W848 class) and rationing-mode standing orders (scheduled top-ups, alternate sourcing); after-action review captures utility performance and storage-capacity lessons feeding W692&#x27;s tracking
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager / BCP
Accountable (A): COO Office (rationing mode)
Duration: Post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5561_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5561_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5561_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5561_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-260 (ensure controlled execution — Store Facility &amp; Safety (PA-07.2).) | - operational: restroom-status decisions documented with HSE sign-off; flush-before-restart rule enforced before restroom and food-service reopening; emergency POs reconciled post-event
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5561_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5561_Annotation17" targetRef="W5561_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
